---@class elasticsearch.CatAliases1Request
---@field name string A comma-separated list of aliases to retrieve. Supports wildcards (`*`). To retrieve all aliases, omit this parameter or use `*` or `_all`.
---@field h? elasticsearch.CatTypesCatAliasesColumns A comma-separated list of columns names to display. It supports simple wildcards.
---@field s? elasticsearch.TypesNames List of columns that determine how the table should be sorted. Sorting defaults to ascending and can be changed by setting `:asc` or `:desc` as a suffix to the column name.
---@field expand_wildcards? elasticsearch.TypesExpandWildcards The type of index that wildcard patterns can match. If the request can target data streams, this argument determines whether wildcard expressions match hidden data streams. It supports comma-separated values, such as `open,hidden`.
---@field master_timeout? elasticsearch.TypesDuration The period to wait for a connection to the master node. If the master node is not available before the timeout expires, the request fails and returns an error. To indicated that the request should never timeout, you can set it to `-1`.
---@field format? string Specifies the format to return the columnar data in, can be set to `text`, `json`, `cbor`, `yaml`, or `smile`.
---@field help? boolean When set to `true` will output available columns. This option can't be combined with any other query string option.
---@field v? boolean When set to `true` will enable verbose output.
---@field bytes? elasticsearch.TypesBytes|string Sets the units for columns that contain a byte-size value. Note that byte-size value units work in terms of powers of 1024. For instance `1kb` means 1024 bytes, not 1000 bytes. If omitted, byte-size values are rendered with a suffix such as `kb`, `mb`, or `gb`, chosen such that the numeric value of the column is as small as possible whilst still being at least `1.0`. If given, byte-size values are rendered as an integer with no suffix, representing the value of the column in the chosen unit. Values that are not an exact multiple of the chosen unit are rounded down.
---@field time? elasticsearch.TypesTimeUnit|string Sets the units for columns that contain a time duration. If omitted, time duration values are rendered with a suffix such as `ms`, `s`, `m` or `h`, chosen such that the numeric value of the column is as small as possible whilst still being at least `1.0`. If given, time duration values are rendered as an integer with no suffix. Values that are not an exact multiple of the chosen unit are rounded down.

