---@class elasticsearch.CatAllocationAllocationRecord
---@field shards? string Number of primary and replica shards assigned to the node.
---@field shards_undesired? string Amount of shards that are scheduled to be moved elsewhere in the cluster or -1 other than desired balance allocator is used
---@field write_load_forecast? elasticsearch.CatAllocationAllocationRecordWriteLoadForecast Sum of index write load forecasts
---@field disk_indices_forecast? elasticsearch.CatAllocationAllocationRecordDiskIndicesForecast Sum of shard size forecasts
---@field disk_indices? elasticsearch.CatAllocationAllocationRecordDiskIndices Disk space used by the node’s shards. Does not include disk space for the translog or unassigned shards. IMPORTANT: This metric double-counts disk space for hard-linked files, such as those created when shrinking, splitting, or cloning an index.
---@field disk_used? elasticsearch.CatAllocationAllocationRecordDiskUsed Total disk space in use. Elasticsearch retrieves this metric from the node’s operating system (OS). The metric includes disk space for: Elasticsearch, including the translog and unassigned shards; the node’s operating system; any other applications or files on the node. Unlike `disk.indices`, this metric does not double-count disk space for hard-linked files.
---@field disk_avail? elasticsearch.CatAllocationAllocationRecordDiskAvail Free disk space available to Elasticsearch. Elasticsearch retrieves this metric from the node’s operating system. Disk-based shard allocation uses this metric to assign shards to nodes based on available disk space.
---@field disk_total? elasticsearch.CatAllocationAllocationRecordDiskTotal Total disk space for the node, including in-use and available space.
---@field disk_percent? elasticsearch.CatAllocationAllocationRecordDiskPercent Total percentage of disk space in use. Calculated as `disk.used / disk.total`.
---@field host? string Network host for the node. Set using the `network.host` setting.
---@field ip? string IP address and port for the node.
---@field node? string Name for the node. Set using the `node.name` setting.
---@field node_role? string Node roles

