---@class elasticsearch.CatShardsShardsRecord
---@field index? string The index name.
---@field shard? string The shard name.
---@field prirep? string The shard type: `primary` or `replica`.
---@field state? string The shard state. Returned values include: `INITIALIZING`: The shard is recovering from a peer shard or gateway. `RELOCATING`: The shard is relocating. `STARTED`: The shard has started. `UNASSIGNED`: The shard is not assigned to any node.
---@field docs? string The number of documents in the shard.
---@field store? string The disk space used by the shard.
---@field dataset? string total size of dataset (including the cache for partially mounted indices)
---@field ip? string The IP address of the node.
---@field id? string The unique identifier for the node.
---@field node? string The name of node.
---@field sync_id? string The sync identifier.
---@field unassigned_reason? string The reason for the last change to the state of an unassigned shard. It does not explain why the shard is currently unassigned; use the cluster allocation explain API for that information. Returned values include: `ALLOCATION_FAILED`: Unassigned as a result of a failed allocation of the shard. `CLUSTER_RECOVERED`: Unassigned as a result of a full cluster recovery. `DANGLING_INDEX_IMPORTED`: Unassigned as a result of importing a dangling index. `EXISTING_INDEX_RESTORED`: Unassigned as a result of restoring into a closed index. `FORCED_EMPTY_PRIMARY`: The shard’s allocation was last modified by forcing an empty primary using the cluster reroute API. `INDEX_CLOSED`: Unassigned because the index was closed. `INDEX_CREATED`: Unassigned as a result of an API creation of an index. `INDEX_REOPENED`: Unassigned as a result of opening a closed index. `MANUAL_ALLOCATION`: The shard’s allocation was last modified by the cluster reroute API. `NEW_INDEX_RESTORED`: Unassigned as a result of restoring into a new index. `NODE_LEFT`: Unassigned as a result of the node hosting it leaving the cluster. `NODE_RESTARTING`: Similar to `NODE_LEFT`, except that the node was registered as restarting using the node shutdown API. `PRIMARY_FAILED`: The shard was initializing as a replica, but the primary shard failed before the initialization completed. `REALLOCATED_REPLICA`: A better replica location is identified and causes the existing replica allocation to be cancelled. `REINITIALIZED`: When a shard moves from started back to initializing. `REPLICA_ADDED`: Unassigned as a result of explicit addition of a replica. `REROUTE_CANCELLED`: Unassigned as a result of explicit cancel reroute command.
---@field unassigned_at? string The time at which the shard became unassigned in Coordinated Universal Time (UTC).
---@field unassigned_for? string The time at which the shard was requested to be unassigned in Coordinated Universal Time (UTC).
---@field unassigned_details? string Additional details as to why the shard became unassigned. It does not explain why the shard is not assigned; use the cluster allocation explain API for that information.
---@field recoverysource_type? string The type of recovery source.
---@field completion_size? string The size of completion.
---@field fielddata_memory_size? string The used fielddata cache memory.
---@field fielddata_evictions? string The fielddata cache evictions.
---@field query_cache_memory_size? string The used query cache memory.
---@field query_cache_evictions? string The query cache evictions.
---@field flush_total? string The number of flushes.
---@field flush_total_time? string The time spent in flush.
---@field get_current? string The number of current get operations.
---@field get_time? string The time spent in get operations.
---@field get_total? string The number of get operations.
---@field get_exists_time? string The time spent in successful get operations.
---@field get_exists_total? string The number of successful get operations.
---@field get_missing_time? string The time spent in failed get operations.
---@field get_missing_total? string The number of failed get operations.
---@field indexing_delete_current? string The number of current deletion operations.
---@field indexing_delete_time? string The time spent in deletion operations.
---@field indexing_delete_total? string The number of delete operations.
---@field indexing_index_current? string The number of current indexing operations.
---@field indexing_index_time? string The time spent in indexing operations.
---@field indexing_index_total? string The number of indexing operations.
---@field indexing_index_failed? string The number of failed indexing operations.
---@field merges_current? string The number of current merge operations.
---@field merges_current_docs? string The number of current merging documents.
---@field merges_current_size? string The size of current merge operations.
---@field merges_total? string The number of completed merge operations.
---@field merges_total_docs? string The nuber of merged documents.
---@field merges_total_size? string The size of current merges.
---@field merges_total_time? string The time spent merging documents.
---@field refresh_total? string The total number of refreshes.
---@field refresh_time? string The time spent in refreshes.
---@field refresh_external_total? string The total nunber of external refreshes.
---@field refresh_external_time? string The time spent in external refreshes.
---@field refresh_listeners? string The number of pending refresh listeners.
---@field search_fetch_current? string The current fetch phase operations.
---@field search_fetch_time? string The time spent in fetch phase.
---@field search_fetch_total? string The total number of fetch operations.
---@field search_open_contexts? string The number of open search contexts.
---@field search_query_current? string The current query phase operations.
---@field search_query_time? string The time spent in query phase.
---@field search_query_total? string The total number of query phase operations.
---@field search_scroll_current? string The open scroll contexts.
