---@class elasticsearch.CatTransformsTransformsRecord
---@field id? string The transform identifier.
---@field state? string The status of the transform. Returned values include: `aborting`: The transform is aborting. `failed: The transform failed. For more information about the failure, check the `reason` field. `indexing`: The transform is actively processing data and creating new documents. `started`: The transform is running but not actively indexing data. `stopped`: The transform is stopped. `stopping`: The transform is stopping.
---@field checkpoint? string The sequence number for the checkpoint.
---@field documents_processed? string The number of documents that have been processed from the source index of the transform.
---@field checkpoint_progress? string The progress of the next checkpoint that is currently in progress.
---@field last_search_time? string The timestamp of the last search in the source indices. This field is shown only if the transform is running.
---@field changes_last_detection_time? string The timestamp when changes were last detected in the source indices.
---@field create_time? string The time the transform was created.
---@field version? string The version of Elasticsearch that existed on the node when the transform was created.
---@field source_index? string The source indices for the transform.
---@field dest_index? string The destination index for the transform.
---@field pipeline? string The unique identifier for the ingest pipeline.
---@field description? string The description of the transform.
---@field transform_type? string The type of transform: `batch` or `continuous`.
---@field frequency? string The interval between checks for changes in the source indices when the transform is running continuously.
---@field max_page_search_size? string The initial page size that is used for the composite aggregation for each checkpoint.
---@field docs_per_second? string The number of input documents per second.
---@field reason? string If a transform has a `failed` state, these details describe the reason for failure.
---@field search_total? string The total number of search operations on the source index for the transform.
---@field search_failure? string The total number of search failures.
---@field search_time? string The total amount of search time, in milliseconds.
---@field index_total? string The total number of index operations done by the transform.
---@field index_failure? string The total number of indexing failures.
---@field index_time? string The total time spent indexing documents, in milliseconds.
---@field documents_indexed? string The number of documents that have been indexed into the destination index for the transform.
---@field delete_time? string The total time spent deleting documents, in milliseconds.
---@field documents_deleted? string The number of documents deleted from the destination index due to the retention policy for the transform.
---@field trigger_count? string The number of times the transform has been triggered by the scheduler. For example, the scheduler triggers the transform indexer to check for updates or ingest new data at an interval specified in the `frequency` property.
---@field pages_processed? string The number of search or bulk index operations processed. Documents are processed in batches instead of individually.
---@field processing_time? string The total time spent processing results, in milliseconds.
---@field checkpoint_duration_time_exp_avg? string The exponential moving average of the duration of the checkpoint, in milliseconds.
---@field indexed_documents_exp_avg? string The exponential moving average of the number of new documents that have been indexed.
---@field processed_documents_exp_avg? string The exponential moving average of the number of documents that have been processed.

