---@class elasticsearch.CcrPutAutoFollowPatternRequest
---@field name string The name of the collection of auto-follow patterns.
---@field master_timeout? elasticsearch.TypesDuration Period to wait for a connection to the master node.
---@field remote_cluster string The remote cluster containing the leader indices to match against.
---@field follow_index_pattern? string The name of follower index. The template {{leader_index}} can be used to derive the name of the follower index from the name of the leader index. When following a data stream, use {{leader_index}}; CCR does not support changes to the names of a follower data stream’s backing indices.
---@field leader_index_patterns? elasticsearch.TypesIndexPatterns An array of simple index patterns to match against indices in the remote cluster specified by the remote_cluster field.
---@field leader_index_exclusion_patterns? elasticsearch.TypesIndexPatterns An array of simple index patterns that can be used to exclude indices from being auto-followed. Indices in the remote cluster whose names are matching one or more leader_index_patterns and one or more leader_index_exclusion_patterns won’t be followed.
---@field max_outstanding_read_requests? number The maximum number of outstanding reads requests from the remote cluster.
---@field settings? elasticsearch.CcrPutAutoFollowPatternRequestSettingsMap Settings to override from the leader index. Note that certain settings can not be overrode (e.g., index.number_of_shards).
---@field max_outstanding_write_requests? number The maximum number of outstanding reads requests from the remote cluster.
---@field read_poll_timeout? elasticsearch.TypesDuration The maximum time to wait for new operations on the remote cluster when the follower index is synchronized with the leader index. When the timeout has elapsed, the poll for operations will return to the follower so that it can update some statistics. Then the follower will immediately attempt to read from the leader again.
---@field max_read_request_operation_count? number The maximum number of operations to pull per read from the remote cluster.
---@field max_read_request_size? elasticsearch.TypesByteSize The maximum size in bytes of per read of a batch of operations pulled from the remote cluster.
---@field max_retry_delay? elasticsearch.TypesDuration The maximum time to wait before retrying an operation that failed exceptionally. An exponential backoff strategy is employed when retrying.
---@field max_write_buffer_count? number The maximum number of operations that can be queued for writing. When this limit is reached, reads from the remote cluster will be deferred until the number of queued operations goes below the limit.
---@field max_write_buffer_size? elasticsearch.TypesByteSize The maximum total bytes of operations that can be queued for writing. When this limit is reached, reads from the remote cluster will be deferred until the total bytes of queued operations goes below the limit.
---@field max_write_request_operation_count? number The maximum number of operations per bulk write request executed on the follower.
---@field max_write_request_size? elasticsearch.TypesByteSize The maximum total bytes of operations per bulk write request executed on the follower.

