---@class elasticsearch.ClusterStatsCCSUsageClusterStats
---@field total number The total number of successful (not skipped) cross-cluster search requests that were executed against this cluster. This may include requests where partial results were returned, but not requests in which the cluster has been skipped entirely.
---@field skipped number The total number of cross-cluster search requests for which this cluster was skipped.
---@field took elasticsearch.ClusterStatsCCSUsageTimeValue Statistics about the time taken to execute requests against this cluster.

---@class elasticsearch.ClusterStatsCCSUsageStats
---@field total number The total number of cross-cluster search requests that have been executed by the cluster.
---@field success number The total number of cross-cluster search requests that have been successfully executed by the cluster.
---@field skipped number The total number of cross-cluster search requests (successful or failed) that had at least one remote cluster skipped.
---@field took elasticsearch.ClusterStatsCCSUsageTimeValue Statistics about the time taken to execute cross-cluster search requests.
---@field took_mrt_true? elasticsearch.ClusterStatsCCSUsageTimeValue Statistics about the time taken to execute cross-cluster search requests for which the `ccs_minimize_roundtrips` setting was set to `true`.
---@field took_mrt_false? elasticsearch.ClusterStatsCCSUsageTimeValue Statistics about the time taken to execute cross-cluster search requests for which the `ccs_minimize_roundtrips` setting was set to `false`.
---@field remotes_per_search_max number The maximum number of remote clusters that were queried in a single cross-cluster search request.
---@field remotes_per_search_avg number The average number of remote clusters that were queried in a single cross-cluster search request.
---@field failure_reasons elasticsearch.ClusterStatsCCSUsageStatsFailureReasonsMap Statistics about the reasons for cross-cluster search request failures. The keys are the failure reason names and the values are the number of requests that failed for that reason.
---@field features elasticsearch.ClusterStatsCCSUsageStatsFeaturesMap The keys are the names of the search feature, and the values are the number of requests that used that feature. Single request can use more than one feature (e.g. both `async` and `wildcard`).
---@field clients elasticsearch.ClusterStatsCCSUsageStatsClientsMap Statistics about the clients that executed cross-cluster search requests. The keys are the names of the clients, and the values are the number of requests that were executed by that client. Only known clients (such as `kibana` or `elasticsearch`) are counted.
---@field clusters elasticsearch.ClusterStatsCCSUsageStatsClustersMap Statistics about the clusters that were queried in cross-cluster search requests. The keys are cluster names, and the values are per-cluster telemetry data. This also includes the local cluster itself, which uses the name `(local)`.

