---@class elasticsearch.EqlGetStatusResponse
---@field id string Identifier for the search.
---@field is_partial boolean If true, the search request is still executing. If false, the search is completed.
---@field is_running boolean If true, the response does not contain complete search results. This could be because either the search is still running (is_running status is false), or because it is already completed (is_running status is true) and results are partial due to failures or timeouts.
---@field start_time_in_millis? number For a running search shows a timestamp when the eql search started, in milliseconds since the Unix epoch.
---@field expiration_time_in_millis? number Shows a timestamp when the eql search will be expired, in milliseconds since the Unix epoch. When this time is reached, the search and its results are deleted, even if the search is still ongoing.
---@field completion_status? number For a completed search shows the http status code of the completed search.

---@class elasticsearch.EqlSearch1Request
---@field index string Comma-separated list of index names to scope the operation
---@field allow_no_indices? boolean A setting that does two separate checks on the index expression. If `false`, the request returns an error (1) if any wildcard expression (including `_all` and `*`) resolves to zero matching indices or (2) if the complete set of resolved indices, aliases or data streams is empty after all expressions are evaluated. If `true`, index expressions that resolve to no indices are allowed and the request returns an empty result.
---@field allow_partial_search_results? boolean If true, returns partial results if there are shard failures. If false, returns an error with no partial results.
---@field allow_partial_sequence_results? boolean If true, sequence queries will return partial results in case of shard failures. If false, they will return no results at all. This flag has effect only if allow_partial_search_results is true.
---@field expand_wildcards? elasticsearch.TypesExpandWildcards Whether to expand wildcard expression to concrete indices that are open, closed or both.
---@field ccs_minimize_roundtrips? boolean Indicates whether network round-trips should be minimized as part of cross-cluster search requests execution
---@field ignore_unavailable? boolean If `false`, the request returns an error if it targets a concrete (non-wildcarded) index, alias, or data stream that is missing, closed, or otherwise unavailable. If `true`, unavailable concrete targets are silently ignored.
---@field keep_alive? elasticsearch.TypesDuration Period for which the search and its results are stored on the cluster.
---@field keep_on_completion? boolean If true, the search and its results are stored on the cluster.
---@field wait_for_completion_timeout? elasticsearch.TypesDuration Timeout duration to wait for the request to finish. Defaults to no timeout, meaning the request waits for complete search results.
---@field query string EQL query you wish to run.
---@field case_sensitive? boolean
---@field event_category_field? string Field containing the event classification, such as process, file, or network.
---@field tiebreaker_field? string Field used to sort hits with the same timestamp in ascending order
---@field timestamp_field? string Field containing event timestamp.
---@field fetch_size? number Maximum number of events to search at a time for sequence queries.
---@field filter? elasticsearch.EqlSearch1RequestFilter Query, written in Query DSL, used to filter the events on which the EQL query runs.
---@field size? number For basic queries, the maximum number of matching events to return. Defaults to 10
---@field fields? elasticsearch.EqlSearch1RequestFields Array of wildcard (*) patterns. The response returns values for field names matching these patterns in the fields property of each hit.
---@field result_position? elasticsearch.EqlSearchResultPosition|string
---@field runtime_mappings? elasticsearch.TypesMappingRuntimeFields
---@field max_samples_per_key? number By default, the response of a sample query contains up to `10` samples, with one sample per unique set of join keys. Use the `size` parameter to get a smaller or larger set of samples. To retrieve more than one sample per set of join keys, use the `max_samples_per_key` parameter. Pipes are not supported for sample queries.

---Array of wildcard (*) patterns. The response returns values for field names matching these patterns in the fields property of each hit.
