---It defaults to an empty map.
---If a name matches a dynamic template, that template will be applied regardless of other match predicates defined in the template.
---If a field is already defined in the mapping, then this parameter won't be used.
---@alias elasticsearch.GlobalBulkIndexOperationDynamicTemplatesMap { [string]: string }

---An action line, which is the first line of each operation in a bulk request.
---It specifies the action to perform (`index`, `create`, `update`, or `delete`) and its metadata, such as the target index and document ID.
---All actions except `delete` expect a source line to follow.
---@class elasticsearch.GlobalBulkOperationContainer
---@field index? elasticsearch.GlobalBulkIndexOperation Index the specified document. If the document exists, it replaces the document and increments the version. The following line must contain the source data to be indexed.
---@field create? elasticsearch.GlobalBulkCreateOperation Index the specified document if it does not already exist. The following line must contain the source data to be indexed.
---@field update? elasticsearch.GlobalBulkUpdateOperation Perform a partial document update. The following line must contain the partial document and update options.
---@field delete? elasticsearch.GlobalBulkDeleteOperation Remove the specified document from the index.

---@class elasticsearch.GlobalBulkResponseItem
---@field _id? string The document ID associated with the operation.
---@field _index string The name of the index associated with the operation. If the operation targeted a data stream, this is the backing index into which the document was written.
---@field status number The HTTP status code returned for the operation.
---@field failure_store? elasticsearch.GlobalBulkFailureStoreStatus
---@field error? elasticsearch.TypesErrorCause Additional information about the failed operation. The property is returned only for failed operations.
---@field _primary_term? number The primary term assigned to the document for the operation. This property is returned only for successful operations.
---@field result? string The result of the operation. Possible values are `created`, `updated`, `deleted`, `noop`, and `not_found`.
---@field _seq_no? number The sequence number assigned to the document for the operation. Sequence numbers are used to ensure an older version of a document doesn't overwrite a newer version.
---@field _shards? elasticsearch.TypesShardStatistics Shard information for the operation.
---@field _version? number The document version associated with the operation. The document version is incremented each time the document is updated. This property is returned only for successful actions.
---@field forced_refresh? boolean
---@field get? elasticsearch.TypesInlineGetDictUserDefined

---The source line that must follow an `update` action line.
---It specifies the partial document, script, or upsert options to apply, plus optional update settings.
---@class elasticsearch.GlobalBulkUpdateAction
---@field detect_noop? boolean If true, the `result` in the response is set to 'noop' when no changes to the document occur.
---@field doc? any A partial update to an existing document.
---@field doc_as_upsert? boolean Set to `true` to use the contents of `doc` as the value of `upsert`.
---@field script? elasticsearch.TypesScript The script to run to update the document.
---@field scripted_upsert? boolean Set to `true` to run the script whether or not the document exists.
---@field _source? elasticsearch.GlobalSearchTypesSourceConfig If `false`, source retrieval is turned off. You can also specify a comma-separated list of the fields you want to retrieve.
---@field upsert? any If the document does not already exist, the contents of `upsert` are inserted as a new document. If the document exists, the `script` is run.

---@class elasticsearch.GlobalBulkUpdateOperation
---@field _id? string The document ID.
---@field _index? string The name of the index or index alias to perform the action on.
---@field routing? string A custom value used to route operations to a specific shard, or multiple comma separated values. Not allowed when `index.slice.enabled` is `true` for the target index; use `_slice` instead.
---@field if_primary_term? number
---@field if_seq_no? number
---@field version? number
---@field version_type? elasticsearch.TypesVersionType|string
---@field require_alias? boolean If `true`, the request's actions must target an index alias.
---@field retry_on_conflict? number The number of times an update should be retried in the case of a version conflict.

