---@field visit_percentage? number The percentage of postings to visit, from 0 to 100. `0` selects the automatic visit calculation.
---@field num_candidates? number The number of nearest neighbor candidates to consider per shard. It can't be less than `k`, or more than 10000 (9999 with sampling).
---@field rescore_vector? elasticsearch.TypesRescoreVector The rescoring of the candidates. Only applies to quantized fields.
---@field exact? boolean If `true`, compares every vector at full precision. Only applies to the `baseline`, requires `allow_exact_baseline`, and can't be combined with other settings.
---@field rescore_window_capped? boolean If `true`, the number of vectors to rescore exceeded the limit of 10000.
---@field quantized_scores? boolean If `true`, the hits were not rescored, so their scores are estimates, and no query is excluded from the mean recall.

