---@field highlight? elasticsearch.GlobalSearchTypesHighlight Specifies the highlighter to use for retrieving highlighted snippets from one or more fields in your search results.
---@field track_total_hits? elasticsearch.GlobalSearchTypesTrackHits Number of hits matching the query to count accurately. If `true`, the exact number of hits is returned at the cost of some performance. If `false`, the response does not include the total number of hits matching the query.
---@field indices_boost? elasticsearch.GlobalSearchTypesSearchRequestBodyIndicesBoostList Boost the `_score` of documents from specified indices. The boost value is the factor by which scores are multiplied. A boost value greater than `1.0` increases the score. A boost value between `0` and `1.0` decreases the score.
---@field docvalue_fields? elasticsearch.GlobalSearchTypesSearchRequestBodyDocvalueFieldsList An array of wildcard (`*`) field patterns. The request returns doc values for field names matching these patterns in the `hits.fields` property of the response.
---@field knn? elasticsearch.GlobalSearchTypesSearchRequestBodyKnn The approximate kNN search to run.
---@field rank? elasticsearch.TypesRankContainer The Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF) to use.
---@field min_score? number The minimum `_score` for matching documents. Documents with a lower `_score` are not included in search results or results collected by aggregations.
---@field post_filter? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslQueryContainer Use the `post_filter` parameter to filter search results. The search hits are filtered after the aggregations are calculated. A post filter has no impact on the aggregation results.
---@field profile? boolean Set to `true` to return detailed timing information about the execution of individual components in a search request. NOTE: This is a debugging tool and adds significant overhead to search execution.
---@field query? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslQueryContainer The search definition using the Query DSL.
---@field rescore? elasticsearch.GlobalSearchTypesSearchRequestBodyRescore Can be used to improve precision by reordering just the top (for example 100 - 500) documents returned by the `query` and `post_filter` phases.
---@field retriever? elasticsearch.TypesRetrieverContainer A retriever is a specification to describe top documents returned from a search. A retriever replaces other elements of the search API that also return top documents such as `query` and `knn`.
---@field script_fields? elasticsearch.GlobalSearchTypesSearchRequestBodyScriptFieldsMap Retrieve a script evaluation (based on different fields) for each hit.
---@field search_after? elasticsearch.TypesSortResults Used to retrieve the next page of hits using a set of sort values from the previous page.
---@field size? number The number of hits to return, which must not be negative. By default, you cannot page through more than 10,000 hits using the `from` and `size` parameters. To page through more hits, use the `search_after` property.
---@field slice? elasticsearch.TypesSlicedScroll Split a scrolled search into multiple slices that can be consumed independently.
---@field sort? elasticsearch.TypesSort A comma-separated list of <field>:<direction> pairs.
---@field _source? elasticsearch.GlobalSearchTypesSourceConfig The source fields that are returned for matching documents. These fields are returned in the `hits._source` property of the search response. If the `stored_fields` property is specified, the `_source` property defaults to `false`. Otherwise, it defaults to `true`.
---@field fields? elasticsearch.GlobalSearchTypesSearchRequestBodyFieldsList An array of wildcard (`*`) field patterns. The request returns values for field names matching these patterns in the `hits.fields` property of the response.
---@field suggest? elasticsearch.GlobalSearchTypesSuggester Defines a suggester that provides similar looking terms based on a provided text.
---@field terminate_after? number The maximum number of documents to collect for each shard. If a query reaches this limit, Elasticsearch terminates the query early. Elasticsearch collects documents before sorting. IMPORTANT: Use with caution. Elasticsearch applies this property to each shard handling the request. When possible, let Elasticsearch perform early termination automatically. Avoid specifying this property for requests that target data streams with backing indices across multiple data tiers. If set to `0` (default), the query does not terminate early.
---@field timeout? string The period of time to wait for a response from each shard. If no response is received before the timeout expires, the request fails and returns an error. Defaults to no timeout.
---@field track_scores? boolean If `true`, calculate and return document scores, even if the scores are not used for sorting.
---@field version? boolean If `true`, the request returns the document version as part of a hit.
---@field seq_no_primary_term? boolean If `true`, the request returns sequence number and primary term of the last modification of each hit.
---@field stored_fields? elasticsearch.TypesFields A comma-separated list of stored fields to return as part of a hit. If no fields are specified, no stored fields are included in the response. If this field is specified, the `_source` property defaults to `false`. You can pass `_source: true` to return both source fields and stored fields in the search response.
---@field pit? elasticsearch.GlobalSearchTypesPointInTimeReference Limit the search to a point in time (PIT). If you provide a PIT, you cannot specify an `<index>` in the request path.
---@field runtime_mappings? elasticsearch.TypesMappingRuntimeFields One or more runtime fields in the search request. These fields take precedence over mapped fields with the same name.
---@field stats? elasticsearch.GlobalSearchTypesSearchRequestBodyStatsList The stats groups to associate with the search. Each group maintains a statistics aggregation for its associated searches. You can retrieve these stats using the indices stats API.

