---@class elasticsearch.IndicesSegmentsSegment
---@field attributes? elasticsearch.IndicesSegmentsSegmentAttributesMap Contains information about whether high compression was enabled and per-field vector formats.
---@field committed boolean If `true`, the segment is synced to disk. Segments that are synced can survive a hard reboot. If `false`, the data from uncommitted segments is also stored in the transaction log so that Elasticsearch is able to replay changes on the next start.
---@field compound? boolean If `true`, Lucene merged all files from the segment into a single file to save file descriptors.
---@field deleted_docs number The number of deleted documents as reported by Lucene, which may be higher or lower than the number of delete operations you have performed. This number excludes deletes that were performed recently and do not yet belong to a segment. Deleted documents are cleaned up by the automatic merge process if it makes sense to do so. Also, Elasticsearch creates extra deleted documents to internally track the recent history of operations on a shard.
---@field generation number Generation number, such as `0`. Elasticsearch increments this generation number for each segment written then uses this number to derive the segment name.
---@field search boolean If `true`, the segment is searchable. If `false`, the segment has most likely been written to disk but needs a refresh to be searchable.
---@field merge_id? string The ID of the merge the segment is part of. Only returned while the segment is being merged.
---@field sort? elasticsearch.IndicesSegmentsSegmentSortList The index sort of the segment. Only returned when the index is sorted.
---@field size? elasticsearch.TypesByteSize Disk space used by the segment.
---@field size_in_bytes number Disk space used by the segment, in bytes.
---@field num_docs number The number of documents as reported by Lucene. This excludes deleted documents and counts any nested documents separately from their parents. It also excludes documents which were indexed recently and do not yet belong to a segment.
---@field version? string Version of Lucene used to write the segment.
---@field auto_calibration? elasticsearch.IndicesSegmentsSegmentAutoCalibrationMap The auto-calibration information of the segment, per `dense_vector` field that supports auto-calibration. Only returned when `include_auto_calibration` is `true`.

