---@class elasticsearch.IndicesTypesDataStream
---@field _meta? elasticsearch.TypesMetadata Custom metadata for the stream, copied from the `_meta` object of the stream’s matching index template. If empty, the response omits this property.
---@field allow_custom_routing? boolean If `true`, the data stream allows custom routing on write request.
---@field failure_store? elasticsearch.IndicesTypesFailureStore Information about failure store backing indices
---@field generation number Current generation for the data stream. This number acts as a cumulative count of the stream’s rollovers, starting at 1.
---@field hidden boolean If `true`, the data stream is hidden.
---@field ilm_policy? string Name of the current ILM lifecycle policy in the stream’s matching index template. This lifecycle policy is set in the `index.lifecycle.name` setting. If the template does not include a lifecycle policy, this property is not included in the response. NOTE: A data stream’s backing indices may be assigned different lifecycle policies. To retrieve the lifecycle policy for individual backing indices, use the get index settings API.
---@field next_generation_managed_by elasticsearch.IndicesTypesManagedBy Name of the lifecycle system that'll manage the next generation of the data stream.
---@field prefer_ilm boolean Indicates if ILM should take precedence over DSL in case both are configured to managed this data stream.
---@field indices elasticsearch.IndicesTypesDataStreamIndicesList Array of objects containing information about the data stream’s backing indices. The last item in this array contains information about the stream’s current write index.
---@field lifecycle? elasticsearch.IndicesTypesDataStreamLifecycleWithRollover Contains the configuration for the data stream lifecycle of this data stream.
---@field name string Name of the data stream.
---@field replicated? boolean If `true`, the data stream is created and managed by cross-cluster replication and the local cluster can not write into this data stream or change its mappings.
---@field rollover_on_write boolean If `true`, the next write to this data stream will trigger a rollover first and the document will be indexed in the new backing index. If the rollover fails the indexing request will fail too.
---@field settings elasticsearch.IndicesTypesIndexSettings The settings specific to this data stream that will take precedence over the settings in the matching index template.
---@field mappings? elasticsearch.TypesMappingTypeMapping The mappings specific to this data stream that will take precedence over the mappings in the matching index template.
---@field status elasticsearch.TypesHealthStatus Health status of the data stream. This health status is based on the state of the primary and replica shards of the stream’s backing indices.
---@field system? boolean If `true`, the data stream is created and managed by an Elastic stack component and cannot be modified through normal user interaction.
---@field template string Name of the index template used to create the data stream’s backing indices. The template’s index pattern must match the name of this data stream.
---@field timestamp_field elasticsearch.IndicesTypesDataStreamTimestampField Information about the `@timestamp` field in the data stream.
---@field index_mode? elasticsearch.IndicesTypesIndexMode The index mode for the data stream that will be used for newly created backing indices.

---Data stream failure store contains the configuration of the failure store for a given data stream.
---@class elasticsearch.IndicesTypesDataStreamFailureStore
---@field enabled? boolean If defined, it turns the failure store on/off (`true`/`false`) for this data stream. A data stream failure store that's disabled (enabled: `false`) will redirect no new failed indices to the failure store; however, it will not remove any existing data from the failure store.
---@field lifecycle? elasticsearch.IndicesTypesFailureStoreLifecycle If defined, it specifies the lifecycle configuration for the failure store of this data stream.

