---Data stream lifecycle denotes that a data stream is managed by the data stream lifecycle and contains the configuration.
---@class elasticsearch.IndicesTypesDataStreamLifecycle
---@field data_retention? elasticsearch.TypesDuration If defined, every document added to this data stream will be stored at least for this time frame. Any time after this duration the document could be deleted. When empty, every document in this data stream will be stored indefinitely.
---@field effective_retention? elasticsearch.TypesDuration The least amount of time data should be kept by elasticsearch.
---@field retention_determined_by? elasticsearch.IndicesTypesRetentionSource|string Configuration source that can influence the retention of a data stream.
---@field downsampling? elasticsearch.IndicesTypesDataStreamLifecycleDownsamplingList The list of downsampling rounds to execute as part of this downsampling configuration
---@field downsampling_method? elasticsearch.IndicesTypesSamplingMethod|string The method used to downsample the data. There are two options `aggregate` and `last_value`. It requires `downsampling` to be defined. Defaults to `aggregate`.
---@field enabled? boolean If defined, it turns data stream lifecycle on/off (`true`/`false`) for this data stream. A data stream lifecycle that's disabled (enabled: `false`) will have no effect on the data stream.
---@field frozen_after? elasticsearch.TypesDuration The period after which data stream backing indices are automatically converted to partially mounted searchable snapshots. This field is valid only on main data stream lifecycles and cannot be set on failure-store lifecycles.

