---@class elasticsearch.IndicesTypesSoftDeletes
---@field enabled? boolean Indicates whether soft deletes are enabled on the index.
---@field retention_lease? elasticsearch.IndicesTypesRetentionLease The maximum period to retain a shard history retention lease before it is considered expired. Shard history retention leases ensure that soft deletes are retained during merges on the Lucene index. If a soft delete is merged away before it can be replicated to a follower the following process will fail due to incomplete history on the leader.

---@alias elasticsearch.IndicesTypesSourceMode "disabled"|"stored"|"synthetic"

---@class elasticsearch.IndicesTypesStorage
---@field type? elasticsearch.IndicesTypesStorageType
---@field allow_mmap? boolean You can restrict the use of the mmapfs and the related hybridfs store type via the setting node.store.allow_mmap. This is a boolean setting indicating whether or not memory-mapping is allowed. The default is to allow it. This setting is useful, for example, if you are in an environment where you can not control the ability to create a lot of memory maps so you need disable the ability to use memory-mapping.
---@field stats_refresh_interval? elasticsearch.TypesDuration How often store statistics are refreshed

---@alias elasticsearch.IndicesTypesStorageType elasticsearch.IndicesTypesStorageTypeCase0|string|string

---@alias elasticsearch.IndicesTypesStorageTypeCase0 "fs"|"niofs"|"mmapfs"|"hybridfs"

---@class elasticsearch.IndicesTypesTranslog
---@field sync_interval? elasticsearch.TypesDuration How often the translog is fsynced to disk and committed, regardless of write operations. Values less than 100ms are not allowed.
---@field durability? elasticsearch.IndicesTypesTranslogDurability|string Whether or not to `fsync` and commit the translog after every index, delete, update, or bulk request.
---@field flush_threshold_size? elasticsearch.TypesByteSize The translog stores all operations that are not yet safely persisted in Lucene (i.e., are not part of a Lucene commit point). Although these operations are available for reads, they will need to be replayed if the shard was stopped and had to be recovered. This setting controls the maximum total size of these operations, to prevent recoveries from taking too long. Once the maximum size has been reached a flush will happen, generating a new Lucene commit point.
---@field retention? elasticsearch.IndicesTypesTranslogRetention

---@alias elasticsearch.IndicesTypesTranslogDurability "request"|"REQUEST"|"async"|"ASYNC"

---@class elasticsearch.IndicesTypesTranslogRetention
---@field size? elasticsearch.TypesByteSize This controls the total size of translog files to keep for each shard. Keeping more translog files increases the chance of performing an operation based sync when recovering a replica. If the translog files are not sufficient, replica recovery will fall back to a file based sync. This setting is ignored, and should not be set, if soft deletes are enabled. Soft deletes are enabled by default in indices created in Elasticsearch versions 7.0.0 and later.
---@field age? elasticsearch.TypesDuration This controls the maximum duration for which translog files are kept by each shard. Keeping more translog files increases the chance of performing an operation based sync when recovering replicas. If the translog files are not sufficient, replica recovery will fall back to a file based sync. This setting is ignored, and should not be set, if soft deletes are enabled. Soft deletes are enabled by default in indices created in Elasticsearch versions 7.0.0 and later.

---@class elasticsearch.IndicesUpdateAliasesAction
---@field add? elasticsearch.IndicesUpdateAliasesAddAction Adds a data stream or index to an alias. If the alias doesn’t exist, the `add` action creates it.
---@field remove? elasticsearch.IndicesUpdateAliasesRemoveAction Removes a data stream or index from an alias.
---@field remove_index? elasticsearch.IndicesUpdateAliasesRemoveIndexAction Deletes an index. You cannot use this action on aliases or data streams.

---@class elasticsearch.IndicesUpdateAliasesAddAction
---@field alias? string Alias for the action. Index alias names support date math.
---@field aliases? elasticsearch.IndicesUpdateAliasesAddActionAliases Aliases for the action. Index alias names support date math.
---@field filter? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslQueryContainer Query used to limit documents the alias can access.
