---@class elasticsearch.InferenceNonStreamingChatCompletionRequest
---@field inference_id string The inference Id
---@field timeout? elasticsearch.TypesDuration Specifies the amount of time to wait for the inference request to complete.
---@field messages elasticsearch.InferenceNonStreamingChatCompletionRequestMessagesList A list of objects representing the conversation. Requests should generally only add new messages from the user (role `user`). The other message roles (`assistant`, `system`, or `tool`) should generally only be copied from the response to a previous completion request, such that the messages array is built up throughout a conversation.
---@field model? string The ID of the model to use. By default, the model ID is set to the value included when creating the inference endpoint.
---@field max_completion_tokens? number The upper bound limit for the number of tokens that can be generated for a completion request.
---@field reasoning? elasticsearch.InferenceTypesReasoning The reasoning configuration for the completion request. This controls the model's reasoning process in one of two ways: * By specifying the model’s reasoning effort level with the `effort` field. * By enabling reasoning with default settings by setting `enabled` field to `true`. It also includes optional settings to control: * The level of detail in the summary returned in the response with the `summary` field. * Whether reasoning details are included in the response at all with the `exclude` field. Example (effort): ``` { "reasoning": { "effort": "high", "summary": "concise", "exclude": false } } ``` Example (enabled): ``` { "reasoning": { "enabled": true, "summary": "concise", "exclude": false } } ``` Currently supported only for `elastic` provider.
---@field cache_control? elasticsearch.InferenceTypesCacheControl The prompt caching configuration for the completion request. Example: ``` { "cache_control": { "type": "ephemeral", "ttl": "1h" } } ``` Unknown fields in the object and invalid `ttl` values return an error. Currently supported only for `elastic` provider.
---@field session_id? string An identifier that groups related completion requests into a session. Currently supported only for `elastic` provider.
---@field stop? elasticsearch.InferenceNonStreamingChatCompletionRequestStopList A sequence of strings to control when the model should stop generating additional tokens.
---@field temperature? number The sampling temperature to use.
---@field tool_choice? elasticsearch.InferenceTypesCompletionToolType Controls which tool is called by the model. String representation: One of `auto`, `none`, or `requrired`. `auto` allows the model to choose between calling tools and generating a message. `none` causes the model to not call any tools. `required` forces the model to call one or more tools. Example (object representation): ``` { "tool_choice": { "type": "function", "function": { "name": "get_current_weather" } } } ```
---@field tools? elasticsearch.InferenceNonStreamingChatCompletionRequestToolsList A list of tools that the model can call. Example: ``` { "tools": [ { "type": "function", "function": { "name": "get_price_of_item", "description": "Get the current price of an item", "parameters": { "type": "object", "properties": { "item": { "id": "12345" }, "unit": { "type": "currency" } } } } } ] } ```
---@field top_p? number Nucleus sampling, an alternative to sampling with temperature.

---A list of objects representing the conversation.
---Requests should generally only add new messages from the user (role `user`).
---The other message roles (`assistant`, `system`, or `tool`) should generally only be copied from the response to a previous completion request, such that the messages array is built up throughout a conversation.
---@alias elasticsearch.InferenceNonStreamingChatCompletionRequestMessagesList elasticsearch.InferenceTypesMessage[]

---A sequence of strings to control when the model should stop generating additional tokens.
---@alias elasticsearch.InferenceNonStreamingChatCompletionRequestStopList string[]

---A list of tools that the model can call.
---Example:
---```
---{
---  "tools": [
---      {
---          "type": "function",
---          "function": {
---              "name": "get_price_of_item",
---              "description": "Get the current price of an item",
---              "parameters": {
---                  "type": "object",
---                  "properties": {
---                      "item": {
---                          "id": "12345"
---                      },
---                      "unit": {
---                          "type": "currency"
---                      }
---                  }
---              }
---          }
---      }
---  ]
---}
---```
---@alias elasticsearch.InferenceNonStreamingChatCompletionRequestToolsList elasticsearch.InferenceTypesCompletionTool[]

