---@class elasticsearch.IngestTypesProcessorContainer
---@field append? elasticsearch.IngestTypesAppendProcessor Appends one or more values to an existing array if the field already exists and it is an array. Converts a scalar to an array and appends one or more values to it if the field exists and it is a scalar. Creates an array containing the provided values if the field doesn’t exist. Accepts a single value or an array of values.
---@field attachment? elasticsearch.IngestTypesAttachmentProcessor The attachment processor lets Elasticsearch extract file attachments in common formats (such as PPT, XLS, and PDF) by using the Apache text extraction library Tika.
---@field bytes? elasticsearch.IngestTypesBytesProcessor Converts a human readable byte value (for example `1kb`) to its value in bytes (for example `1024`). If the field is an array of strings, all members of the array will be converted. Supported human readable units are "b", "kb", "mb", "gb", "tb", "pb" case insensitive. An error will occur if the field is not a supported format or resultant value exceeds 2^63.
---@field cef? elasticsearch.IngestTypesCefProcessor Converts a CEF message into a structured format.
---@field circle? elasticsearch.IngestTypesCircleProcessor Converts circle definitions of shapes to regular polygons which approximate them.
---@field community_id? elasticsearch.IngestTypesCommunityIDProcessor Computes the Community ID for network flow data as defined in the Community ID Specification. You can use a community ID to correlate network events related to a single flow.
---@field convert? elasticsearch.IngestTypesConvertProcessor Converts a field in the currently ingested document to a different type, such as converting a string to an integer. If the field value is an array, all members will be converted.
---@field csv? elasticsearch.IngestTypesCsvProcessor Extracts fields from CSV line out of a single text field within a document. Any empty field in CSV will be skipped.
---@field date? elasticsearch.IngestTypesDateProcessor Parses dates from fields, and then uses the date or timestamp as the timestamp for the document.
---@field date_index_name? elasticsearch.IngestTypesDateIndexNameProcessor The purpose of this processor is to point documents to the right time based index based on a date or timestamp field in a document by using the date math index name support.
---@field dissect? elasticsearch.IngestTypesDissectProcessor Extracts structured fields out of a single text field by matching the text field against a delimiter-based pattern.
---@field dot_expander? elasticsearch.IngestTypesDotExpanderProcessor Expands a field with dots into an object field. This processor allows fields with dots in the name to be accessible by other processors in the pipeline. Otherwise these fields can’t be accessed by any processor.
---@field drop? elasticsearch.IngestTypesDropProcessor Drops the document without raising any errors. This is useful to prevent the document from getting indexed based on some condition.
---@field enrich? elasticsearch.IngestTypesEnrichProcessor The `enrich` processor can enrich documents with data from another index.
---@field fail? elasticsearch.IngestTypesFailProcessor Raises an exception. This is useful for when you expect a pipeline to fail and want to relay a specific message to the requester.
---@field fingerprint? elasticsearch.IngestTypesFingerprintProcessor Computes a hash of the document’s content. You can use this hash for content fingerprinting.
---@field foreach? elasticsearch.IngestTypesForeachProcessor Runs an ingest processor on each element of an array or object.
---@field ip_location? elasticsearch.IngestTypesIpLocationProcessor Currently an undocumented alias for GeoIP Processor.
---@field geo_grid? elasticsearch.IngestTypesGeoGridProcessor Converts geo-grid definitions of grid tiles or cells to regular bounding boxes or polygons which describe their shape. This is useful if there is a need to interact with the tile shapes as spatially indexable fields.
---@field geoip? elasticsearch.IngestTypesGeoIpProcessor The `geoip` processor adds information about the geographical location of an IPv4 or IPv6 address.
---@field grok? elasticsearch.IngestTypesGrokProcessor Extracts structured fields out of a single text field within a document. You choose which field to extract matched fields from, as well as the grok pattern you expect will match. A grok pattern is like a regular expression that supports aliased expressions that can be reused.
---@field gsub? elasticsearch.IngestTypesGsubProcessor Converts a string field by applying a regular expression and a replacement. If the field is an array of string, all members of the array will be converted. If any non-string values are encountered, the processor will throw an exception.
---@field html_strip? elasticsearch.IngestTypesHtmlStripProcessor Removes HTML tags from the field. If the field is an array of strings, HTML tags will be removed from all members of the array.
---@field inference? elasticsearch.IngestTypesInferenceProcessor Uses a pre-trained data frame analytics model or a model deployed for natural language processing tasks to infer against the data that is being ingested in the pipeline.
---@field join? elasticsearch.IngestTypesJoinProcessor Joins each element of an array into a single string using a separator character between each element. Throws an error when the field is not an array.
---@field json? elasticsearch.IngestTypesJsonProcessor Parses a string containing JSON data into a structured object, string, or other value.
---@field kv? elasticsearch.IngestTypesKeyValueProcessor This processor helps automatically parse messages (or specific event fields) which are of the `foo=bar` variety.
---@field lowercase? elasticsearch.IngestTypesLowercaseProcessor Converts a string to its lowercase equivalent. If the field is an array of strings, all members of the array will be converted.
---@field network_direction? elasticsearch.IngestTypesNetworkDirectionProcessor Calculates the network direction given a source IP address, destination IP address, and a list of internal networks.
---@field normalize_for_stream? elasticsearch.IngestTypesNormalizeForStreamProcessor Detects whether a document is OpenTelemetry-compliant and, if not, normalizes it so that it can be queried by clients that expect either ECS or OpenTelemetry Semantic Conventions formats.
---@field pipeline? elasticsearch.IngestTypesPipelineProcessor Executes another pipeline.
---@field recover_failure_document? elasticsearch.IngestTypesRecoverFailureDocumentProcessor Recovers documents that have been stored in a data stream's failure store by restoring them to their original format.
---@field redact? elasticsearch.IngestTypesRedactProcessor The Redact processor uses the Grok rules engine to obscure text in the input document matching the given Grok patterns. The processor can be used to obscure Personal Identifying Information (PII) by configuring it to detect known patterns such as email or IP addresses. Text that matches a Grok pattern is replaced with a configurable string such as `<EMAIL>` where an email address is matched or simply replace all matches with the text `<REDACTED>` if preferred.
---@field registered_domain? elasticsearch.IngestTypesRegisteredDomainProcessor Extracts the registered domain (also known as the effective top-level domain or eTLD), sub-domain, and top-level domain from a fully qualified domain name (FQDN). Uses the registered domains defined in the Mozilla Public Suffix List.
---@field remove? elasticsearch.IngestTypesRemoveProcessor Removes existing fields. If one field doesn’t exist, an exception will be thrown.
---@field rename? elasticsearch.IngestTypesRenameProcessor Renames an existing field. If the field doesn’t exist or the new name is already used, an exception will be thrown.
---@field reroute? elasticsearch.IngestTypesRerouteProcessor Routes a document to another target index or data stream. When setting the `destination` option, the target is explicitly specified and the dataset and namespace options can’t be set. When the `destination` option is not set, this processor is in a data stream mode. Note that in this mode, the reroute processor can only be used on data streams that follow the data stream naming scheme.
---@field script? elasticsearch.IngestTypesScriptProcessor Runs an inline or stored script on incoming documents. The script runs in the `ingest` context.
---@field set? elasticsearch.IngestTypesSetProcessor Adds a field with the specified value. If the field already exists, its value will be replaced with the provided one.
---@field set_security_user? elasticsearch.IngestTypesSetSecurityUserProcessor Sets user-related details (such as `username`, `roles`, `email`, `full_name`, `metadata`, `api_key`, `realm` and `authentication_type`) from the current authenticated user to the current document by pre-processing the ingest.
---@field sort? elasticsearch.IngestTypesSortProcessor Sorts the elements of an array ascending or descending. Homogeneous arrays of numbers will be sorted numerically, while arrays of strings or heterogeneous arrays of strings + numbers will be sorted lexicographically. Throws an error when the field is not an array.
---@field split? elasticsearch.IngestTypesSplitProcessor Splits a field into an array using a separator character. Only works on string fields.
---@field terminate? elasticsearch.IngestTypesTerminateProcessor Terminates the current ingest pipeline, causing no further processors to be run. This will normally be executed conditionally, using the `if` option.
---@field trim? elasticsearch.IngestTypesTrimProcessor Trims whitespace from a field. If the field is an array of strings, all members of the array will be trimmed. This only works on leading and trailing whitespace.
---@field uppercase? elasticsearch.IngestTypesUppercaseProcessor Converts a string to its uppercase equivalent. If the field is an array of strings, all members of the array will be converted.
---@field urldecode? elasticsearch.IngestTypesUrlDecodeProcessor URL-decodes a string. If the field is an array of strings, all members of the array will be decoded.
---@field uri_parts? elasticsearch.IngestTypesUriPartsProcessor Parses a Uniform Resource Identifier (URI) string and extracts its components as an object. This URI object includes properties for the URI’s domain, path, fragment, port, query, scheme, user info, username, and password.
---@field user_agent? elasticsearch.IngestTypesUserAgentProcessor The `user_agent` processor extracts details from the user agent string a browser sends with its web requests. This processor adds this information by default under the `user_agent` field.

