---@class elasticsearch.InvalidateSecuritySamlRequest
---@field acs? string The Assertion Consumer Service URL that matches the one of the SAML realm in Elasticsearch that should be used. You must specify either this parameter or the `realm` parameter.
---@field query_string string The query part of the URL that the user was redirected to by the SAML IdP to initiate the Single Logout. This query should include a single parameter named `SAMLRequest` that contains a SAML logout request that is deflated and Base64 encoded. If the SAML IdP has signed the logout request, the URL should include two extra parameters named `SigAlg` and `Signature` that contain the algorithm used for the signature and the signature value itself. In order for Elasticsearch to be able to verify the IdP's signature, the value of the `query_string` field must be an exact match to the string provided by the browser. The client application must not attempt to parse or process the string in any way.
---@field realm? string The name of the SAML realm in Elasticsearch the configuration. You must specify either this parameter or the `acs` parameter.

---@class elasticsearch.InvalidateSecuritySamlResponse
---@field invalidated number The number of tokens that were invalidated as part of this logout.
---@field realm string The realm name of the SAML realm in Elasticsearch that authenticated the user.
---@field redirect string A SAML logout response as a parameter so that the user can be redirected back to the SAML IdP.

---@class elasticsearch.KnnEval1Request
---@field index string A comma-separated list of index names to search.
---@field ignore_unavailable? boolean If `false`, the request returns an error if it targets a missing or closed index.
---@field allow_no_indices? boolean If `false`, the request returns an error if any wildcard expression, index alias, or `_all` value targets only missing or closed indices. This behavior applies even if the request targets other open indices.
---@field expand_wildcards? elasticsearch.TypesExpandWildcards The type of index that wildcard patterns can match. It supports comma-separated values, such as `open,hidden`.
---@field wait_for_completion? boolean If `true`, the request waits for the evaluation to complete. A large evaluation can run for minutes, and closing the connection, for example because of a client or proxy timeout, cancels it. If `false`, the request returns a task identifier, and stores the completed response for retrieval through the task management API.
---@field field string The `dense_vector` field to evaluate.
---@field k number The number of nearest neighbors to compute the recall for, from 1 to 1000.
---@field query_source elasticsearch.GlobalKnnEvalKnnEvalQuerySource The source of the query vectors.
---@field baseline? elasticsearch.GlobalKnnEvalKnnEvalSettings The settings of the search that the `knn_settings` entries are compared with. If not specified, it uses a `visit_percentage` of 20 and a `rescore_vector.oversample` of 100.
---@field knn_settings elasticsearch.KnnEval1RequestKnnSettingsList The kNN search settings to evaluate, from 1 to 32 unique entries.
---@field allow_exact_baseline? boolean If `true`, the `baseline` can be `exact`. An exact baseline compares every vector at full precision, and can severely slow down other searches.

