---@field metadata? any An object map that contains metadata about the model.
---@field model_type? elasticsearch.MlTypesTrainedModelType|string The model type.
---@field model_size_bytes? number The estimated memory usage in bytes to keep the trained model in memory. This property is supported only if defer_definition_decompression is true or the model definition is not supplied.
---@field platform_architecture? string The platform architecture (if applicable) of the trained mode. If the model only works on one platform, because it is heavily optimized for a particular processor architecture and OS combination, then this field specifies which. The format of the string must match the platform identifiers used by Elasticsearch, so one of, `linux-x86_64`, `linux-aarch64`, `darwin-aarch64`, or `windows-x86_64`. For portable models (those that work independent of processor architecture or OS features), leave this field unset.
---@field tags? elasticsearch.MlPutTrainedModelRequestTagsList An array of tags to organize the model.
---@field prefix_strings? elasticsearch.MlTypesTrainedModelPrefixStrings Optional prefix strings applied at inference

