---@class elasticsearch.MlTypesDataframeAnalytics
---@field analysis_stats? elasticsearch.MlTypesDataframeAnalyticsStatsContainer An object containing information about the analysis job.
---@field assignment_explanation? string For running jobs only, contains messages relating to the selection of a node to run the job.
---@field data_counts elasticsearch.MlTypesDataframeAnalyticsStatsDataCounts An object that provides counts for the quantity of documents skipped, used in training, or available for testing.
---@field id string The unique identifier of the data frame analytics job.
---@field memory_usage elasticsearch.MlTypesDataframeAnalyticsStatsMemoryUsage An object describing memory usage of the analytics. It is present only after the job is started and memory usage is reported.
---@field node? elasticsearch.TypesNodeAttributes Contains properties for the node that runs the job. This information is available only for running jobs.
---@field progress elasticsearch.MlTypesDataframeAnalyticsProgressList The progress report of the data frame analytics job by phase.
---@field state elasticsearch.MlTypesDataframeState The status of the data frame analytics job, which can be one of the following values: failed, started, starting, stopping, stopped.

---@class elasticsearch.MlTypesDataframeAnalyticsAuthorization
---@field api_key? elasticsearch.MlTypesApiKeyAuthorization If an API key was used for the most recent update to the job, its name and identifier are listed in the response.
---@field roles? elasticsearch.MlTypesDataframeAnalyticsAuthorizationRolesList If a user ID was used for the most recent update to the job, its roles at the time of the update are listed in the response.
---@field service_account? string If a service account was used for the most recent update to the job, the account name is listed in the response.

---If a user ID was used for the most recent update to the job, its roles at the time of the update are listed in the response.
