---@field name string The field name.
---@field reason? string The reason a field is not selected to be included in the analysis.

---The mapping types of the field.
---@alias elasticsearch.MlTypesDataframeAnalyticsFieldSelectionMappingTypesList string[]

---@class elasticsearch.MlTypesDataframeAnalyticsMemoryEstimation
---@field expected_memory_with_disk string Estimated memory usage under the assumption that overflowing to disk is allowed during data frame analytics. expected_memory_with_disk is usually smaller than expected_memory_without_disk as using disk allows to limit the main memory needed to perform data frame analytics.
---@field expected_memory_without_disk string Estimated memory usage under the assumption that the whole data frame analytics should happen in memory (i.e. without overflowing to disk).

---The progress report of the data frame analytics job by phase.
---@alias elasticsearch.MlTypesDataframeAnalyticsProgressList elasticsearch.MlTypesDataframeAnalyticsStatsProgress[]

---@class elasticsearch.MlTypesDataframeAnalyticsSource
---@field index elasticsearch.TypesIndices Index or indices on which to perform the analysis. It can be a single index or index pattern as well as an array of indices or patterns. NOTE: If your source indices contain documents with the same IDs, only the document that is indexed last appears in the destination index.
---@field query? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslQueryContainer The Elasticsearch query domain-specific language (DSL). This value corresponds to the query object in an Elasticsearch search POST body. All the options that are supported by Elasticsearch can be used, as this object is passed verbatim to Elasticsearch. By default, this property has the following value: {"match_all": {}}.
---@field runtime_mappings? elasticsearch.TypesMappingRuntimeFields Definitions of runtime fields that will become part of the mapping of the destination index.
---@field _source? elasticsearch.MlTypesDataframeAnalysisAnalyzedFields Specify `includes` and/or `excludes patterns to select which fields will be present in the destination. Fields that are excluded cannot be included in the analysis.

---@class elasticsearch.MlTypesDataframeAnalyticsStatsContainer
---@field classification_stats? elasticsearch.MlTypesDataframeAnalyticsStatsHyperparameters An object containing information about the classification analysis job.
---@field outlier_detection_stats? elasticsearch.MlTypesDataframeAnalyticsStatsOutlierDetection An object containing information about the outlier detection job.
---@field regression_stats? elasticsearch.MlTypesDataframeAnalyticsStatsHyperparameters An object containing information about the regression analysis.

---@class elasticsearch.MlTypesDataframeAnalyticsStatsDataCounts
---@field skipped_docs_count number The number of documents that are skipped during the analysis because they contained values that are not supported by the analysis. For example, outlier detection does not support missing fields so it skips documents with missing fields. Likewise, all types of analysis skip documents that contain arrays with more than one element.
---@field test_docs_count number The number of documents that are not used for training the model and can be used for testing.
---@field training_docs_count number The number of documents that are used for training the model.

---@class elasticsearch.MlTypesDataframeAnalyticsStatsHyperparameters
---@field hyperparameters elasticsearch.MlTypesHyperparameters An object containing the parameters of the classification analysis job.
---@field iteration number The number of iterations on the analysis.
---@field timestamp number The timestamp when the statistics were reported in milliseconds since the epoch.
---@field timing_stats elasticsearch.MlTypesTimingStats An object containing time statistics about the data frame analytics job.
---@field validation_loss elasticsearch.MlTypesValidationLoss An object containing information about validation loss.

---@class elasticsearch.MlTypesDataframeAnalyticsStatsMemoryUsage
---@field memory_reestimate_bytes? number This value is present when the status is hard_limit and it is a new estimate of how much memory the job needs.
---@field peak_usage_bytes number The number of bytes used at the highest peak of memory usage.
---@field status string The memory usage status.
