---@class elasticsearch.PutTransformRequest
---@field transform_id string Identifier for the transform. This identifier can contain lowercase alphanumeric characters (a-z and 0-9), hyphens, and underscores. It has a 64 character limit and must start and end with alphanumeric characters.
---@field defer_validation? boolean When the transform is created, a series of validations occur to ensure its success. For example, there is a check for the existence of the source indices and a check that the destination index is not part of the source index pattern. You can use this parameter to skip the checks, for example when the source index does not exist until after the transform is created. The validations are always run when you start the transform, however, with the exception of privilege checks.
---@field timeout? elasticsearch.TypesDuration Period to wait for a response. If no response is received before the timeout expires, the request fails and returns an error.
---@field dest elasticsearch.TransformTypesDestination The destination for the transform.
---@field description? string Free text description of the transform.
---@field frequency? elasticsearch.TypesDuration The interval between checks for changes in the source indices when the transform is running continuously. Also determines the retry interval in the event of transient failures while the transform is searching or indexing. The minimum value is `1s` and the maximum is `1h`.
---@field latest? elasticsearch.TransformTypesLatest The latest method transforms the data by finding the latest document for each unique key.
---@field _meta? elasticsearch.TypesMetadata Defines optional transform metadata.
---@field pivot? elasticsearch.TransformTypesPivot The pivot method transforms the data by aggregating and grouping it. These objects define the group by fields and the aggregation to reduce the data.
---@field retention_policy? elasticsearch.TransformTypesRetentionPolicyContainer Defines a retention policy for the transform. Data that meets the defined criteria is deleted from the destination index.
---@field settings? elasticsearch.TransformTypesSettings Defines optional transform settings.
---@field source elasticsearch.TransformTypesSource The source of the data for the transform.
---@field sync? elasticsearch.TransformTypesSyncContainer Defines the properties transforms require to run continuously.

