---@class elasticsearch.ReindexRethrottleRequest
---@field task_id string The task identifier, returned when creating a reindex task, or by listing tasks via `GET /_reindex` or `GET /_tasks`. In stack, can be either the original task ID or the task ID of the relocated task.
---@field requests_per_second number The maximum number of documents to index per second, across the entire reindex operation (including slices). It can be either `-1` to turn off throttling or any decimal number like `1.7` or `12` to throttle to that level.
---@field group_by? elasticsearch.TasksTypesGroupBy|string The way to group the tasks in the response. We recommend setting this to `none`, which provides the cleanest response format.

---@class elasticsearch.ReindexRethrottleResponse
---@field node_failures? elasticsearch.ReindexRethrottleResponseNodeFailuresList Node-level failures encountered while applying the rethrottle request. Will return a `failed_node_exception` wrapping a `no_such_node_exception`, if a node handling the task either never existed, or has left the cluster, and one of the following is true: 1. The task has completed. 2. The task cannot be found. Note: Rethrottle handles relocations, so it should succeed if the task can be found and has not completed.
---@field task_failures? elasticsearch.ReindexRethrottleResponseTaskFailuresList Per-task failures encountered while applying the rethrottle. If a rethrottle is attempted during a relocation handoff, the failure object reports `status: SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE` (the HTTP response itself is still `200 OK`). In this case, the request can be retried until success.
---@field nodes? elasticsearch.ReindexRethrottleResponseNodesMap Tasks grouped by node, returned only when `group_by=nodes` (the default).
---@field tasks? elasticsearch.GlobalReindexRethrottleReindexTasks The tasks that were successfully rethrottled. Always returned in serverless. Returned with `group_by=none` or `group_by=parents` in stack.

