---@field _source? elasticsearch.GlobalSearchTypesSourceConfigParam The source fields that are returned for matching documents. These fields are returned in the `hits._source` property of the search response. Valid values are: * `true` to return the entire document source. * `false` to not return the document source. * `<string>` to return the source fields that are specified as a comma-separated list that supports wildcard (`*`) patterns.
---@field _source_excludes? elasticsearch.TypesFields A comma-separated list of source fields to exclude from the response. You can also use this parameter to exclude fields from the subset specified in `_source_includes` query parameter. If the `_source` parameter is `false`, this parameter is ignored.
---@field _source_exclude_vectors? boolean Whether vectors should be excluded from _source
---@field _source_includes? elasticsearch.TypesFields A comma-separated list of source fields to include in the response. If this parameter is specified, only these source fields are returned. You can exclude fields from this subset using the `_source_excludes` query parameter. If the `_source` parameter is `false`, this parameter is ignored.
---@field seq_no_primary_term? boolean If `true`, the request returns the sequence number and primary term of the last modification of each hit.
---@field q? string A query in the Lucene query string syntax. Query parameter searches do not support the full Elasticsearch Query DSL but are handy for testing. IMPORTANT: This parameter overrides the query parameter in the request body. If both parameters are specified, documents matching the query request body parameter are not returned.
---@field size? number The number of hits to return. By default, you cannot page through more than 10,000 hits using the `from` and `size` parameters. To page through more hits, use the `search_after` parameter.
---@field from? number The starting document offset, which must be non-negative. By default, you cannot page through more than 10,000 hits using the `from` and `size` parameters. To page through more hits, use the `search_after` parameter.
---@field sort? elasticsearch.Search3RequestSort A comma-separated list of `<field>:<direction>` pairs.
---@field aggregations? elasticsearch.Search3RequestAggregationsMap Defines the aggregations that are run as part of the search request.
---@field collapse? elasticsearch.GlobalSearchTypesFieldCollapse Collapses search results the values of the specified field.
---@field ext? elasticsearch.Search3RequestExtMap Configuration of search extensions defined by Elasticsearch plugins.
---@field highlight? elasticsearch.GlobalSearchTypesHighlight Specifies the highlighter to use for retrieving highlighted snippets from one or more fields in your search results.
---@field indices_boost? elasticsearch.Search3RequestIndicesBoostList Boost the `_score` of documents from specified indices. The boost value is the factor by which scores are multiplied. A boost value greater than `1.0` increases the score. A boost value between `0` and `1.0` decreases the score.
---@field knn? elasticsearch.Search3RequestKnn The approximate kNN search to run.
---@field rank? elasticsearch.TypesRankContainer The Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF) to use.
---@field min_score? number The minimum `_score` for matching documents. Documents with a lower `_score` are not included in search results and results collected by aggregations.
---@field post_filter? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslQueryContainer Use the `post_filter` parameter to filter search results. The search hits are filtered after the aggregations are calculated. A post filter has no impact on the aggregation results.
---@field profile? boolean Set to `true` to return detailed timing information about the execution of individual components in a search request. NOTE: This is a debugging tool and adds significant overhead to search execution.
---@field query? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslQueryContainer The search definition using the Query DSL.
---@field rescore? elasticsearch.Search3RequestRescore Can be used to improve precision by reordering just the top (for example 100 - 500) documents returned by the `query` and `post_filter` phases.
---@field retriever? elasticsearch.TypesRetrieverContainer A retriever is a specification to describe top documents returned from a search. A retriever replaces other elements of the search API that also return top documents such as `query` and `knn`.
---@field script_fields? elasticsearch.Search3RequestScriptFieldsMap Retrieve a script evaluation (based on different fields) for each hit.
---@field search_after? elasticsearch.TypesSortResults Used to retrieve the next page of hits using a set of sort values from the previous page.
---@field slice? elasticsearch.TypesSlicedScroll Split a scrolled search into multiple slices that can be consumed independently.
---@field fields? elasticsearch.Search3RequestFieldsList An array of wildcard (`*`) field patterns. The request returns values for field names matching these patterns in the `hits.fields` property of the response.
---@field suggest? elasticsearch.GlobalSearchTypesSuggester Defines a suggester that provides similar looking terms based on a provided text.
---@field pit? elasticsearch.GlobalSearchTypesPointInTimeReference Limit the search to a point in time (PIT). If you provide a PIT, you cannot specify an `<index>` in the request path.
---@field runtime_mappings? elasticsearch.TypesMappingRuntimeFields One or more runtime fields in the search request. These fields take precedence over mapped fields with the same name.

