---@class elasticsearch.SearchMvt1Request
---@field index string A list of indices, data streams, or aliases to search. It supports wildcards (`*`). To search all data streams and indices, omit this parameter or use `*` or `_all`. To search a remote cluster, use the `<cluster>:<target>` syntax.
---@field field string A field that contains the geospatial data to return. It must be a `geo_point` or `geo_shape` field. The field must have doc values enabled. It cannot be a nested field. NOTE: Vector tiles do not natively support geometry collections. For `geometrycollection` values in a `geo_shape` field, the API returns a hits layer feature for each element of the collection. This behavior may change in a future release.
---@field zoom number The zoom level of the vector tile to search. It accepts `0` to `29`.
---@field x number The X coordinate for the vector tile to search.
---@field y number The Y coordinate for the vector tile to search.
---@field exact_bounds? boolean If `false`, the meta layer's feature is the bounding box of the tile. If true, the meta layer's feature is a bounding box resulting from a geo_bounds aggregation. The aggregation runs on <field> values that intersect the <zoom>/<x>/<y> tile with wrap_longitude set to false. The resulting bounding box may be larger than the vector tile.
---@field extent? number The size, in pixels, of a side of the tile. Vector tiles are square with equal sides.
---@field grid_agg? elasticsearch.GlobalSearchMvtTypesGridAggregationType|string Aggregation used to create a grid for `field`.
---@field grid_precision? number Additional zoom levels available through the aggs layer. For example, if <zoom> is 7 and grid_precision is 8, you can zoom in up to level 15. Accepts 0-8. If 0, results don't include the aggs layer.
---@field grid_type? elasticsearch.GlobalSearchMvtTypesGridType|string Determines the geometry type for features in the aggs layer. In the aggs layer, each feature represents a geotile_grid cell. If 'grid' each feature is a Polygon of the cells bounding box. If 'point' each feature is a Point that is the centroid of the cell.
---@field size? number Maximum number of features to return in the hits layer. Accepts 0-10000. If 0, results don't include the hits layer.
---@field track_total_hits? elasticsearch.GlobalSearchTypesTrackHits The number of hits matching the query to count accurately. If `true`, the exact number of hits is returned at the cost of some performance. If `false`, the response does not include the total number of hits matching the query.
---@field with_labels? boolean If `true`, the hits and aggs layers will contain additional point features representing suggested label positions for the original features. * `Point` and `MultiPoint` features will have one of the points selected. * `Polygon` and `MultiPolygon` features will have a single point generated, either the centroid, if it is within the polygon, or another point within the polygon selected from the sorted triangle-tree. * `LineString` features will likewise provide a roughly central point selected from the triangle-tree. * The aggregation results will provide one central point for each aggregation bucket. All attributes from the original features will also be copied to the new label features. In addition, the new features will be distinguishable using the tag `_mvt_label_position`.
---@field aggs? elasticsearch.SearchMvt1RequestAggsMap Sub-aggregations for the geotile_grid. It supports the following aggregation types: - `avg` - `boxplot` - `cardinality` - `extended stats` - `max` - `median absolute deviation` - `min` - `percentile` - `percentile-rank` - `stats` - `sum` - `value count` The aggregation names can't start with `_mvt_`. The `_mvt_` prefix is reserved for internal aggregations.
---@field buffer? number The size, in pixels, of a clipping buffer outside the tile. This allows renderers to avoid outline artifacts from geometries that extend past the extent of the tile.
---@field fields? elasticsearch.TypesFields The fields to return in the `hits` layer. It supports wildcards (`*`). This parameter does not support fields with array values. Fields with array values may return inconsistent results.
---@field query? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslQueryContainer The query DSL used to filter documents for the search.
---@field runtime_mappings? elasticsearch.TypesMappingRuntimeFields Defines one or more runtime fields in the search request. These fields take precedence over mapped fields with the same name.
---@field sort? elasticsearch.TypesSort Sort the features in the hits layer. By default, the API calculates a bounding box for each feature. It sorts features based on this box's diagonal length, from longest to shortest.

---Sub-aggregations for the geotile_grid.
