---@field allow_no_indices? boolean A setting that does two separate checks on the index expression. If `false`, the request returns an error (1) if any wildcard expression (including `_all` and `*`) resolves to zero matching indices or (2) if the complete set of resolved indices, aliases or data streams is empty after all expressions are evaluated. If `true`, index expressions that resolve to no indices are allowed and the request returns an empty result.
---@field ccs_minimize_roundtrips? boolean Indicates whether network round-trips should be minimized as part of cross-cluster search requests execution.
---@field expand_wildcards? elasticsearch.TypesExpandWildcards The type of index that wildcard patterns can match. If the request can target data streams, this argument determines whether wildcard expressions match hidden data streams. Supports comma-separated values, such as `open,hidden`.
---@field explain? boolean If `true`, the response includes additional details about score computation as part of a hit.
---@field ignore_throttled? boolean If `true`, specified concrete, expanded, or aliased indices are not included in the response when throttled.
---@field ignore_unavailable? boolean If `false`, the request returns an error if it targets a concrete (non-wildcarded) index, alias, or data stream that is missing, closed, or otherwise unavailable. If `true`, unavailable concrete targets are silently ignored.
---@field preference? string The node or shard the operation should be performed on. It is random by default.
---@field profile? boolean If `true`, the query execution is profiled.
---@field routing? elasticsearch.TypesRouting A custom value used to route operations to a specific shard. Not allowed when `index.slice.enabled` is `true` for the target index; use `_slice` instead.
---@field scroll? elasticsearch.TypesDuration Specifies how long a consistent view of the index should be maintained for scrolled search.
---@field search_type? elasticsearch.TypesSearchType|string The type of the search operation.
---@field rest_total_hits_as_int? boolean If `true`, `hits.total` is rendered as an integer in the response. If `false`, it is rendered as an object.
---@field typed_keys? boolean If `true`, the response prefixes aggregation and suggester names with their respective types.
---@field id? string The ID of the search template to use. If no `source` is specified, this parameter is required.
---@field params? elasticsearch.SearchTemplate2RequestParamsMap Key-value pairs used to replace Mustache variables in the template. The key is the variable name. The value is the variable value.
---@field source? elasticsearch.TypesScriptSource An inline search template. Supports the same parameters as the search API's request body. It also supports Mustache variables. If no `id` is specified, this parameter is required.

