---@class elasticsearch.SlmPutLifecycleRequest
---@field policy_id string The identifier for the snapshot lifecycle policy you want to create or update.
---@field master_timeout? elasticsearch.TypesDuration The period to wait for a connection to the master node. If no response is received before the timeout expires, the request fails and returns an error. To indicate that the request should never timeout, set it to `-1`.
---@field timeout? elasticsearch.TypesDuration The period to wait for a response. If no response is received before the timeout expires, the request fails and returns an error. To indicate that the request should never timeout, set it to `-1`.
---@field config? elasticsearch.SlmTypesConfiguration Configuration for each snapshot created by the policy.
---@field name? string Name automatically assigned to each snapshot created by the policy. Date math is supported. To prevent conflicting snapshot names, a UUID is automatically appended to each snapshot name.
---@field repository? string Repository used to store snapshots created by this policy. This repository must exist prior to the policy’s creation. You can create a repository using the snapshot repository API.
---@field retention? elasticsearch.SlmTypesRetention Retention rules used to retain and delete snapshots created by the policy.
---@field schedule? string Periodic or absolute schedule at which the policy creates snapshots. SLM applies schedule changes immediately.

---@class elasticsearch.SlmTypesConfiguration
---@field ignore_unavailable? boolean If false, the snapshot fails if any data stream or index in indices is missing or closed. If true, the snapshot ignores missing or closed data streams and indices.
---@field indices? elasticsearch.TypesIndices A comma-separated list of data streams and indices to include in the snapshot. Multi-index syntax is supported. By default, a snapshot includes all data streams and indices in the cluster. If this argument is provided, the snapshot only includes the specified data streams and clusters.
---@field include_global_state? boolean If true, the current global state is included in the snapshot.
---@field feature_states? elasticsearch.SlmTypesConfigurationFeatureStatesList A list of feature states to be included in this snapshot. A list of features available for inclusion in the snapshot and their descriptions be can be retrieved using the get features API. Each feature state includes one or more system indices containing data necessary for the function of that feature. Providing an empty array will include no feature states in the snapshot, regardless of the value of include_global_state. By default, all available feature states will be included in the snapshot if include_global_state is true, or no feature states if include_global_state is false.
---@field metadata? elasticsearch.TypesMetadata Attaches arbitrary metadata to the snapshot, such as a record of who took the snapshot, why it was taken, or any other useful data. Metadata must be less than 1024 bytes.
---@field partial? boolean If false, the entire snapshot will fail if one or more indices included in the snapshot do not have all primary shards available.

---A list of feature states to be included in this snapshot. A list of features available for inclusion in the snapshot and their descriptions be can be retrieved using the get features API.
---Each feature state includes one or more system indices containing data necessary for the function of that feature. Providing an empty array will include no feature states in the snapshot, regardless of the value of include_global_state. By default, all available feature states will be included in the snapshot if include_global_state is true, or no feature states if include_global_state is false.
---@alias elasticsearch.SlmTypesConfigurationFeatureStatesList string[]

