---@class elasticsearch.SnapshotVerifyRepositoryCompactNodeInfo
---@field name string A human-readable name for the node. You can set this name using the `node.name` property in `elasticsearch.yml`. The default value is the machine's hostname.

---@class elasticsearch.SnapshotVerifyRepositoryRequest
---@field repository string The name of the snapshot repository to verify.
---@field master_timeout? elasticsearch.TypesDuration The period to wait for the master node. If the master node is not available before the timeout expires, the request fails and returns an error. To indicate that the request should never timeout, set it to `-1`.
---@field timeout? elasticsearch.TypesDuration The period to wait for a response from all relevant nodes in the cluster after updating the cluster metadata. If no response is received before the timeout expires, the cluster metadata update still applies but the response will indicate that it was not completely acknowledged. To indicate that the request should never timeout, set it to `-1`.

