---@class elasticsearch.StopTransformRequest
---@field transform_id string Identifier for the transform. To stop multiple transforms, use a comma-separated list or a wildcard expression. To stop all transforms, use `_all` or `*` as the identifier.
---@field allow_no_match? boolean Specifies what to do when the request: contains wildcard expressions and there are no transforms that match; contains the `_all` string or no identifiers and there are no matches; contains wildcard expressions and there are only partial matches. If it is true, the API returns a successful acknowledgement message when there are no matches. When there are only partial matches, the API stops the appropriate transforms. If it is false, the request returns a 404 status code when there are no matches or only partial matches.
---@field force? boolean If it is true, the API forcefully stops the transforms.
---@field timeout? elasticsearch.TypesDuration Period to wait for a response when `wait_for_completion` is `true`. If no response is received before the timeout expires, the request returns a timeout exception. However, the request continues processing and eventually moves the transform to a STOPPED state.
---@field wait_for_checkpoint? boolean If it is true, the transform does not completely stop until the current checkpoint is completed. If it is false, the transform stops as soon as possible.
---@field wait_for_completion? boolean If it is true, the API blocks until the indexer state completely stops. If it is false, the API returns immediately and the indexer is stopped asynchronously in the background.

---@class elasticsearch.StopWatcherRequest
---@field master_timeout? elasticsearch.TypesDuration The period to wait for the master node. If the master node is not available before the timeout expires, the request fails and returns an error. To indicate that the request should never timeout, set it to `-1`.

