---@class elasticsearch.TransformScheduleNowTransformRequest
---@field transform_id string Identifier for the transform.
---@field timeout? elasticsearch.TypesDuration Controls the time to wait for the scheduling to take place
---@field defer? boolean When true, defers the scheduling by the transform's configured sync delay instead of triggering immediately. The transform will process new data after the delay elapses rather than right away.

---@class elasticsearch.TransformSetUpgradeModeRequest
---@field enabled? boolean When `true`, it enables `upgrade_mode` which temporarily halts all transform tasks and prohibits new transform tasks from starting.
---@field timeout? elasticsearch.TypesDuration The time to wait for the request to be completed.

---@class elasticsearch.TransformTypesDestination
---@field index? string The destination index for the transform. The mappings of the destination index are deduced based on the source fields when possible. If alternate mappings are required, use the create index API prior to starting the transform.
---@field aliases? elasticsearch.TransformTypesDestinationAliasesList The aliases that the destination index for the transform should have. Aliases are manipulated using the stored credentials of the transform, which means the secondary credentials supplied at creation time (if both primary and secondary credentials are specified). The destination index is added to the aliases regardless of whether the destination index was created by the transform or pre-created by the user.
---@field pipeline? string The unique identifier for an ingest pipeline.

---@class elasticsearch.TransformTypesDestinationAlias
---@field alias string The name of the alias.
---@field move_on_creation? boolean Whether the destination index should be the only index in this alias. If `true`, all the other indices will be removed from this alias before adding the destination index to this alias. This does not delete the removed indices; it only removes them from the alias.

