---@class elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsAggregationContainer
---@field aggregations? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsAggregationContainerAggregationsMap Sub-aggregations for this aggregation. Only applies to bucket aggregations.
---@field meta? elasticsearch.TypesMetadata
---@field adjacency_matrix? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsAdjacencyMatrixAggregation A bucket aggregation returning a form of adjacency matrix. The request provides a collection of named filter expressions, similar to the `filters` aggregation. Each bucket in the response represents a non-empty cell in the matrix of intersecting filters.
---@field auto_date_histogram? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsAutoDateHistogramAggregation A multi-bucket aggregation similar to the date histogram, except instead of providing an interval to use as the width of each bucket, a target number of buckets is provided.
---@field avg? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsAverageAggregation A single-value metrics aggregation that computes the average of numeric values that are extracted from the aggregated documents.
---@field avg_bucket? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsAverageBucketAggregation A sibling pipeline aggregation which calculates the mean value of a specified metric in a sibling aggregation. The specified metric must be numeric and the sibling aggregation must be a multi-bucket aggregation.
---@field boxplot? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsBoxplotAggregation A metrics aggregation that computes a box plot of numeric values extracted from the aggregated documents.
---@field bucket_script? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsBucketScriptAggregation A parent pipeline aggregation which runs a script which can perform per bucket computations on metrics in the parent multi-bucket aggregation.
---@field bucket_selector? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsBucketSelectorAggregation A parent pipeline aggregation which runs a script to determine whether the current bucket will be retained in the parent multi-bucket aggregation.
---@field bucket_sort? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsBucketSortAggregation A parent pipeline aggregation which sorts the buckets of its parent multi-bucket aggregation.
---@field bucket_count_ks_test? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsBucketKsAggregation A sibling pipeline aggregation which runs a two sample Kolmogorov–Smirnov test ("K-S test") against a provided distribution and the distribution implied by the documents counts in the configured sibling aggregation.
---@field bucket_correlation? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsBucketCorrelationAggregation A sibling pipeline aggregation which runs a correlation function on the configured sibling multi-bucket aggregation.
---@field cardinality? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsCardinalityAggregation A single-value metrics aggregation that calculates an approximate count of distinct values.
---@field cartesian_bounds? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsCartesianBoundsAggregation A metric aggregation that computes the spatial bounding box containing all values for a Point or Shape field.
---@field cartesian_centroid? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsCartesianCentroidAggregation A metric aggregation that computes the weighted centroid from all coordinate values for point and shape fields.
---@field categorize_text? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsCategorizeTextAggregation A multi-bucket aggregation that groups semi-structured text into buckets.
---@field change_point? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsChangePointAggregation A sibling pipeline that detects, spikes, dips, and change points in a metric. Given a distribution of values provided by the sibling multi-bucket aggregation, this aggregation indicates the bucket of any spike or dip and/or the bucket at which the largest change in the distribution of values, if they are statistically significant. There must be at least 22 bucketed values. Fewer than 1,000 is preferred.
---@field children? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsChildrenAggregation A single bucket aggregation that selects child documents that have the specified type, as defined in a `join` field.
---@field composite? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsCompositeAggregation A multi-bucket aggregation that creates composite buckets from different sources. Unlike the other multi-bucket aggregations, you can use the `composite` aggregation to paginate *all* buckets from a multi-level aggregation efficiently.
---@field cumulative_cardinality? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsCumulativeCardinalityAggregation A parent pipeline aggregation which calculates the cumulative cardinality in a parent `histogram` or `date_histogram` aggregation.
---@field cumulative_sum? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsCumulativeSumAggregation A parent pipeline aggregation which calculates the cumulative sum of a specified metric in a parent `histogram` or `date_histogram` aggregation.
---@field date_histogram? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsDateHistogramAggregation A multi-bucket values source based aggregation that can be applied on date values or date range values extracted from the documents. It dynamically builds fixed size (interval) buckets over the values.
---@field date_range? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsDateRangeAggregation A multi-bucket value source based aggregation that enables the user to define a set of date ranges - each representing a bucket.
---@field derivative? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsDerivativeAggregation A parent pipeline aggregation which calculates the derivative of a specified metric in a parent `histogram` or `date_histogram` aggregation.
---@field diversified_sampler? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsDiversifiedSamplerAggregation A filtering aggregation used to limit any sub aggregations' processing to a sample of the top-scoring documents. Similar to the `sampler` aggregation, but adds the ability to limit the number of matches that share a common value.
---@field extended_stats? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsExtendedStatsAggregation A multi-value metrics aggregation that computes stats over numeric values extracted from the aggregated documents.
---@field extended_stats_bucket? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsExtendedStatsBucketAggregation A sibling pipeline aggregation which calculates a variety of stats across all bucket of a specified metric in a sibling aggregation.
---@field frequent_item_sets? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsFrequentItemSetsAggregation A bucket aggregation which finds frequent item sets, a form of association rules mining that identifies items that often occur together.
---@field filter? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslQueryContainer A single bucket aggregation that narrows the set of documents to those that match a query.
---@field filters? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsFiltersAggregation A multi-bucket aggregation where each bucket contains the documents that match a query.
---@field geo_bounds? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsGeoBoundsAggregation A metric aggregation that computes the geographic bounding box containing all values for a Geopoint or Geoshape field.
---@field geo_centroid? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsGeoCentroidAggregation A metric aggregation that computes the weighted centroid from all coordinate values for geo fields.
---@field geo_distance? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsGeoDistanceAggregation A multi-bucket aggregation that works on `geo_point` fields. Evaluates the distance of each document value from an origin point and determines the buckets it belongs to, based on ranges defined in the request.
---@field geohash_grid? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsGeoHashGridAggregation A multi-bucket aggregation that groups `geo_point` and `geo_shape` values into buckets that represent a grid. Each cell is labeled using a geohash which is of user-definable precision.
---@field geo_line? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsGeoLineAggregation Aggregates all `geo_point` values within a bucket into a `LineString` ordered by the chosen sort field.
---@field geotile_grid? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsGeoTileGridAggregation A multi-bucket aggregation that groups `geo_point` and `geo_shape` values into buckets that represent a grid. Each cell corresponds to a map tile as used by many online map sites.
---@field geohex_grid? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsGeohexGridAggregation A multi-bucket aggregation that groups `geo_point` and `geo_shape` values into buckets that represent a grid. Each cell corresponds to a H3 cell index and is labeled using the H3Index representation.
---@field ["global"]? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsGlobalAggregation Defines a single bucket of all the documents within the search execution context. This context is defined by the indices and the document types you’re searching on, but is not influenced by the search query itself.
---@field histogram? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsHistogramAggregation A multi-bucket values source based aggregation that can be applied on numeric values or numeric range values extracted from the documents. It dynamically builds fixed size (interval) buckets over the values.
---@field ip_range? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsIpRangeAggregation A multi-bucket value source based aggregation that enables the user to define a set of IP ranges - each representing a bucket.
---@field ip_prefix? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsIpPrefixAggregation A bucket aggregation that groups documents based on the network or sub-network of an IP address.
---@field inference? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsInferenceAggregation A parent pipeline aggregation which loads a pre-trained model and performs inference on the collated result fields from the parent bucket aggregation.
---@field line? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsGeoLineAggregation
---@field matrix_stats? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsMatrixStatsAggregation A numeric aggregation that computes the following statistics over a set of document fields: `count`, `mean`, `variance`, `skewness`, `kurtosis`, `covariance`, and `covariance`.
---@field max? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsMaxAggregation A single-value metrics aggregation that returns the maximum value among the numeric values extracted from the aggregated documents.
---@field max_bucket? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsMaxBucketAggregation A sibling pipeline aggregation which identifies the bucket(s) with the maximum value of a specified metric in a sibling aggregation and outputs both the value and the key(s) of the bucket(s).
---@field median_absolute_deviation? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsMedianAbsoluteDeviationAggregation A single-value aggregation that approximates the median absolute deviation of its search results.
---@field min? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsMinAggregation A single-value metrics aggregation that returns the minimum value among numeric values extracted from the aggregated documents.
---@field min_bucket? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsMinBucketAggregation A sibling pipeline aggregation which identifies the bucket(s) with the minimum value of a specified metric in a sibling aggregation and outputs both the value and the key(s) of the bucket(s).
---@field missing? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsMissingAggregation A field data based single bucket aggregation, that creates a bucket of all documents in the current document set context that are missing a field value (effectively, missing a field or having the configured NULL value set).
---@field moving_avg? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsMovingAverageAggregation
---@field moving_percentiles? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsMovingPercentilesAggregation Given an ordered series of percentiles, "slides" a window across those percentiles and computes cumulative percentiles.
---@field moving_fn? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsMovingFunctionAggregation Given an ordered series of data, "slides" a window across the data and runs a custom script on each window of data. For convenience, a number of common functions are predefined such as `min`, `max`, and moving averages.
---@field multi_terms? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsMultiTermsAggregation A multi-bucket value source based aggregation where buckets are dynamically built - one per unique set of values.
---@field nested? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsNestedAggregation A special single bucket aggregation that enables aggregating nested documents.
---@field normalize? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsNormalizeAggregation A parent pipeline aggregation which calculates the specific normalized/rescaled value for a specific bucket value.
---@field parent? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsParentAggregation A special single bucket aggregation that selects parent documents that have the specified type, as defined in a `join` field.
---@field percentile_ranks? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsPercentileRanksAggregation A multi-value metrics aggregation that calculates one or more percentile ranks over numeric values extracted from the aggregated documents.
---@field percentiles? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsPercentilesAggregation A multi-value metrics aggregation that calculates one or more percentiles over numeric values extracted from the aggregated documents.
---@field percentiles_bucket? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsPercentilesBucketAggregation A sibling pipeline aggregation which calculates percentiles across all bucket of a specified metric in a sibling aggregation.
---@field range? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsRangeAggregation A multi-bucket value source based aggregation that enables the user to define a set of ranges - each representing a bucket.
---@field rare_terms? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsRareTermsAggregation A multi-bucket value source based aggregation which finds "rare" terms — terms that are at the long-tail of the distribution and are not frequent.
---@field rate? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsRateAggregation Calculates a rate of documents or a field in each bucket. Can only be used inside a `date_histogram` or `composite` aggregation.
---@field reverse_nested? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsReverseNestedAggregation A special single bucket aggregation that enables aggregating on parent documents from nested documents. Should only be defined inside a `nested` aggregation.
---@field random_sampler? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsRandomSamplerAggregation A single bucket aggregation that randomly includes documents in the aggregated results. Sampling provides significant speed improvement at the cost of accuracy.
---@field sampler? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsSamplerAggregation A filtering aggregation used to limit any sub aggregations' processing to a sample of the top-scoring documents.
---@field scripted_metric? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsScriptedMetricAggregation A metric aggregation that uses scripts to provide a metric output.
---@field serial_diff? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsSerialDifferencingAggregation An aggregation that subtracts values in a time series from themselves at different time lags or periods.
---@field significant_terms? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsSignificantTermsAggregation Returns interesting or unusual occurrences of terms in a set.
---@field significant_text? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsSignificantTextAggregation Returns interesting or unusual occurrences of free-text terms in a set.
---@field stats? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsStatsAggregation A multi-value metrics aggregation that computes stats over numeric values extracted from the aggregated documents.
---@field stats_bucket? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsStatsBucketAggregation A sibling pipeline aggregation which calculates a variety of stats across all bucket of a specified metric in a sibling aggregation.
---@field string_stats? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsStringStatsAggregation A multi-value metrics aggregation that computes statistics over string values extracted from the aggregated documents.
---@field sum? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsSumAggregation A single-value metrics aggregation that sums numeric values that are extracted from the aggregated documents.
---@field sum_bucket? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsSumBucketAggregation A sibling pipeline aggregation which calculates the sum of a specified metric across all buckets in a sibling aggregation.
---@field terms? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsTermsAggregation A multi-bucket value source based aggregation where buckets are dynamically built - one per unique value.
---@field time_series? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsTimeSeriesAggregation The time series aggregation queries data created using a time series index. This is typically data such as metrics or other data streams with a time component, and requires creating an index using the time series mode.
---@field top_hits? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsTopHitsAggregation A metric aggregation that returns the top matching documents per bucket.
