---@class elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsSignificantTermsAggregation
---@field background_filter? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslQueryContainer A background filter that can be used to focus in on significant terms within a narrower context, instead of the entire index.
---@field chi_square? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsChiSquareHeuristic Use Chi square, as described in "Information Retrieval", Manning et al., Chapter 13.5.2, as the significance score.
---@field exclude? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsTermsExclude Terms to exclude.
---@field execution_hint? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsTermsAggregationExecutionHint|string Mechanism by which the aggregation should be executed: using field values directly or using global ordinals.
---@field field? string The field from which to return significant terms.
---@field gnd? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsGoogleNormalizedDistanceHeuristic Use Google normalized distance as described in "The Google Similarity Distance", Cilibrasi and Vitanyi, 2007, as the significance score.
---@field include? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsTermsInclude Terms to include.
---@field jlh? any Use JLH score as the significance score.
---@field min_doc_count? number Only return terms that are found in more than `min_doc_count` hits.
---@field mutual_information? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsMutualInformationHeuristic Use mutual information as described in "Information Retrieval", Manning et al., Chapter 13.5.1, as the significance score.
---@field percentage? any A simple calculation of the number of documents in the foreground sample with a term divided by the number of documents in the background with the term.
---@field script_heuristic? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsScriptedHeuristic Customized score, implemented via a script.
---@field p_value? elasticsearch.TypesAggregationsPValueHeuristic Significant terms heuristic that calculates the p-value between the term existing in foreground and background sets. The p-value is the probability of obtaining test results at least as extreme as the results actually observed, under the assumption that the null hypothesis is correct. The p-value is calculated assuming that the foreground set and the background set are independent https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bernoulli_trial, with the null hypothesis that the probabilities are the same.
---@field shard_min_doc_count? number Regulates the certainty a shard has if the term should actually be added to the candidate list or not with respect to the `min_doc_count`. Terms will only be considered if their local shard frequency within the set is higher than the `shard_min_doc_count`.
---@field shard_size? number Can be used to control the volumes of candidate terms produced by each shard. By default, `shard_size` will be automatically estimated based on the number of shards and the `size` parameter.
---@field size? number The number of buckets returned out of the overall terms list.

