---@class elasticsearch.TypesMappingDocValuesConfig
---@field multi_value? boolean If `false`, the field is treated as single-valued, enabling optimized storage. Only has an effect when columnar index mode is active.
---@field nullability? boolean If `false`, every document must provide a non-null value for the field: a document that omits the field, sets it to `null`, or supplies only null values (an empty array or an all-null array) is rejected at index time. A field that defines `null_value` is always exempt, since the configured default removes the absence of a value. Only has an effect when columnar index mode is active.

