---An Elasticsearch Query DSL (Domain Specific Language) object that defines a query.
---@class elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslQueryContainer
---@field bool? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslBoolQuery matches documents matching boolean combinations of other queries.
---@field boosting? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslBoostingQuery Returns documents matching a `positive` query while reducing the relevance score of documents that also match a `negative` query.
---@field common? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslQueryContainerCommonMap
---@field combined_fields? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslCombinedFieldsQuery The `combined_fields` query supports searching multiple text fields as if their contents had been indexed into one combined field.
---@field constant_score? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslConstantScoreQuery Wraps a filter query and returns every matching document with a relevance score equal to the `boost` parameter value.
---@field dense_vector? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslDenseVectorQuery Scores every document that has a value for a `dense_vector` field, with the exact similarity between its vector and a query vector. Unlike the `knn` query, it doesn't use an index structure, or a cutoff based on `k` or `num_candidates`.
---@field dis_max? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslDisMaxQuery Returns documents matching one or more wrapped queries, called query clauses or clauses. If a returned document matches multiple query clauses, the `dis_max` query assigns the document the highest relevance score from any matching clause, plus a tie breaking increment for any additional matching subqueries.
---@field distance_feature? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslDistanceFeatureQuery Boosts the relevance score of documents closer to a provided origin date or point. For example, you can use this query to give more weight to documents closer to a certain date or location.
---@field exists? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslExistsQuery Returns documents that contain an indexed value for a field.
---@field function_score? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslFunctionScoreQuery The `function_score` enables you to modify the score of documents that are retrieved by a query.
---@field fuzzy? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslQueryContainerFuzzyMap Returns documents that contain terms similar to the search term, as measured by a Levenshtein edit distance.
---@field geo_bounding_box? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslGeoBoundingBoxQuery Matches geo_point and geo_shape values that intersect a bounding box.
---@field geo_distance? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslGeoDistanceQuery Matches `geo_point` and `geo_shape` values within a given distance of a geopoint.
---@field geo_grid? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslQueryContainerGeoGridMap Matches `geo_point` and `geo_shape` values that intersect a grid cell from a GeoGrid aggregation.
---@field geo_polygon? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslGeoPolygonQuery
---@field geo_shape? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslGeoShapeQuery Filter documents indexed using either the `geo_shape` or the `geo_point` type.
---@field has_child? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslHasChildQuery Returns parent documents whose joined child documents match a provided query.
---@field has_parent? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslHasParentQuery Returns child documents whose joined parent document matches a provided query.
---@field ids? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslIdsQuery Returns documents based on their IDs. This query uses document IDs stored in the `_id` field.
---@field intervals? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslQueryContainerIntervalsMap Returns documents based on the order and proximity of matching terms.
---@field knn? elasticsearch.TypesKnnQuery Finds the k nearest vectors to a query vector, as measured by a similarity metric. knn query finds nearest vectors through approximate search on indexed dense_vectors.
---@field kql? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslKqlQuery Returns documents matching a provided Kibana Query Language (KQL) expression. The expression is parsed and rewritten into standard Query DSL.
---@field match? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslQueryContainerMatchMap Returns documents that match a provided text, number, date or boolean value. The provided text is analyzed before matching.
---@field match_all? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslMatchAllQuery Matches all documents, giving them all a `_score` of 1.0.
---@field match_bool_prefix? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslQueryContainerMatchBoolPrefixMap Analyzes its input and constructs a `bool` query from the terms. Each term except the last is used in a `term` query. The last term is used in a prefix query.
---@field match_none? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslMatchNoneQuery Matches no documents.
---@field match_phrase? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslQueryContainerMatchPhraseMap Analyzes the text and creates a phrase query out of the analyzed text.
---@field match_phrase_prefix? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslQueryContainerMatchPhrasePrefixMap Returns documents that contain the words of a provided text, in the same order as provided. The last term of the provided text is treated as a prefix, matching any words that begin with that term.
---@field more_like_this? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslMoreLikeThisQuery Returns documents that are "like" a given set of documents.
---@field multi_match? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslMultiMatchQuery Enables you to search for a provided text, number, date or boolean value across multiple fields. The provided text is analyzed before matching.
---@field nested? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslNestedQuery Wraps another query to search nested fields. If an object matches the search, the nested query returns the root parent document.
---@field parent_id? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslParentIdQuery Returns child documents joined to a specific parent document.
---@field percolate? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslPercolateQuery Matches queries stored in an index.
---@field pinned? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslPinnedQuery Promotes selected documents to rank higher than those matching a given query.
---@field prefix? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslQueryContainerPrefixMap Returns documents that contain a specific prefix in a provided field.
---@field query_string? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslQueryStringQuery Returns documents based on a provided query string, using a parser with a strict syntax.
---@field range? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslQueryContainerRangeMap Returns documents that contain terms within a provided range.
---@field rank_feature? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslRankFeatureQuery Boosts the relevance score of documents based on the numeric value of a `rank_feature` or `rank_features` field.
---@field regexp? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslQueryContainerRegexpMap Returns documents that contain terms matching a regular expression.
---@field rule? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslRuleQuery
---@field script? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslScriptQuery Filters documents based on a provided script. The script query is typically used in a filter context.
---@field script_score? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslScriptScoreQuery Uses a script to provide a custom score for returned documents.
---@field semantic? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslSemanticQuery A semantic query to semantic_text field types
---@field shape? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslShapeQuery Queries documents that contain fields indexed using the `shape` type.
---@field simple_query_string? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslSimpleQueryStringQuery Returns documents based on a provided query string, using a parser with a limited but fault-tolerant syntax.
---@field span_containing? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslSpanContainingQuery Returns matches which enclose another span query.
---@field span_field_masking? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslSpanFieldMaskingQuery Wrapper to allow span queries to participate in composite single-field span queries by _lying_ about their search field.
---@field span_first? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslSpanFirstQuery Matches spans near the beginning of a field.
---@field span_multi? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslSpanMultiTermQuery Allows you to wrap a multi term query (one of `wildcard`, `fuzzy`, `prefix`, `range`, or `regexp` query) as a `span` query, so it can be nested.
---@field span_near? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslSpanNearQuery Matches spans which are near one another. You can specify `slop`, the maximum number of intervening unmatched positions, as well as whether matches are required to be in-order.
---@field span_not? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslSpanNotQuery Removes matches which overlap with another span query or which are within x tokens before (controlled by the parameter `pre`) or y tokens after (controlled by the parameter `post`) another span query.
---@field span_or? elasticsearch.TypesQueryDslSpanOrQuery Matches the union of its span clauses.
