---@class elasticsearch.UpdateRequest
---@field index string The name of the target index. By default, the index is created automatically if it doesn't exist.
---@field id string A unique identifier for the document to be updated.
---@field if_primary_term? number Only perform the operation if the document has this primary term.
---@field if_seq_no? number Only perform the operation if the document has this sequence number.
---@field include_source_on_error? boolean True or false if to include the document source in the error message in case of parsing errors.
---@field lang? string The script language.
---@field refresh? elasticsearch.TypesRefresh|string If 'true', Elasticsearch refreshes the affected shards to make this operation visible to search. If 'wait_for', it waits for a refresh to make this operation visible to search. If 'false', it does nothing with refreshes.
---@field require_alias? boolean If `true`, the destination must be an index alias.
---@field retry_on_conflict? number The number of times the operation should be retried when a conflict occurs.
---@field routing? elasticsearch.TypesRouting A custom value used to route operations to a specific shard. Not allowed when `index.slice.enabled` is `true` for the target index; use `_slice` instead.
---@field timeout? elasticsearch.TypesDuration The period to wait for the following operations: dynamic mapping updates and waiting for active shards. Elasticsearch waits for at least the timeout period before failing. The actual wait time could be longer, particularly when multiple waits occur.
---@field wait_for_active_shards? elasticsearch.TypesWaitForActiveShards The number of copies of each shard that must be active before proceeding with the operation. Set to 'all' or any positive integer up to the total number of shards in the index (`number_of_replicas`+1). The default value of `1` means it waits for each primary shard to be active.
---@field _source? elasticsearch.GlobalSearchTypesSourceConfigParam If `false`, source retrieval is turned off. You can also specify a comma-separated list of the fields you want to retrieve.
---@field _source_excludes? elasticsearch.TypesFields The source fields you want to exclude.
---@field _source_includes? elasticsearch.TypesFields The source fields you want to retrieve.
---@field detect_noop? boolean If `true`, the `result` in the response is set to `noop` (no operation) when there are no changes to the document.
---@field doc? any A partial update to an existing document. If both `doc` and `script` are specified, `doc` is ignored.
---@field doc_as_upsert? boolean If `true`, use the contents of 'doc' as the value of 'upsert'. NOTE: Using ingest pipelines with `doc_as_upsert` is not supported.
---@field script? elasticsearch.TypesScript The script to run to update the document.
---@field scripted_upsert? boolean If `true`, run the script whether or not the document exists.
---@field upsert? any If the document does not already exist, the contents of 'upsert' are inserted as a new document. If the document exists, the 'script' is run.

